(Kampot): Bokor Mountain is a particularly good tourist destination in Kampot province and there are four main factors that lead to Bokor Mountain can become an important tourist destination in the country and in the world. This was confirmed by Mr. Oknha Say Sophotra, Director of Sales and Marketing, Sokha Hotel and Sokha Real Estate in a meeting with journalists organized by the Club of Cambodian Journalists recently.
These four points are believed by Mr. Say Sophotra that soon, in just five years, this Bokor mountain area will become an important tourist destination in the country and in the world that is suitable for tourism and investment.
In addition, in order to develop along with the conservation of natural resources and the environment in the Bokor Mountains, Sokha Hotel and Sokha Real Estate are studying with Japanese companies to bring techniques to process solid and liquid waste to make it ineffective. Harm to the environment.
Currently, Sokha Hotel and Sokha Real Estate are developing projects such as the construction of a 108-meter-high Buddha statue, the tallest Buddha statue in Asia, residential areas, schools, hospitals, roads and dams. All this does not include the existing historical sites on Bokor Mountain.
According to Duke Sok Kong, he invested about 800 million US dollars to develop on the top of Bokor Mountain. But the $ 800 million spent has yet to be reaped. However, many of the investment projects that the company is developing are to develop Bokor Mountain into a rich tourist destination.
