Analysis: Peace and stability are in the common interest of the countries in the region
BEIJING (Reuters) - Increasing security cooperation in the Asia-Pacific region has recently become a major topic of discussion and discussion at the 21st Sangkrila Dialogue in Singapore. .
In this regard, at the Sangkrila Dialogue, Cambodian Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense Tea Seiha stated that as a member of ASEAN, Cambodia expects countries in the South China Sea to resolve maritime sovereignty disputes peacefully. Through dialogue and agreements, we believe that through the efforts of the parties, ASEAN can find a balanced solution that is acceptable to all parties.
The Asia-Pacific region is a common family of countries in the region. Peace and stability are the common interests of the countries in the region and are an unstoppable current. China will adhere to a close, honest, mutually beneficial environment, expand friendly cooperation with other countries in the region in the common sense, safeguard peace, stability, progress and prosperity that have not been easy to come together. Build a great family.
