ASEAN Committee on Science, Technology and Innovation Collaborates with Stakeholders to Hold Workshop on "Capturing Human-Based Artificial Intelligence"
(Siem Reap): The ASEAN Committee on Science, Technology and Innovation, in collaboration with the Asia Foundation and the Institute for Human Intelligence at Stanford University, USA, has organized a workshop on "Capturing Human-Based Artificial Intelligence Technology".
The workshop was held on June 3, 2024, in conjunction with the 20th ASEAN Ministerial Meeting on Science, Technology and Innovation (AMMSTI-20), the 85th Meeting of the ASEAN Committee on Science, Technology and Innovation (COSTI- 85) and related meetings that are being held in Siem Reap from 3-7 June 2024.
The discussion was chaired by Mr. Hul Seangheng, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and Chair of the ASEAN Committee on Science, Technology and Innovation, with about 160 participants from ASEAN Member States and a delegation of ASEAN scientists and technicians. America.
Discussions focused on emerging artificial intelligence technologies, including challenges, the need for AI tools and knowledge, and the development of responsible AI policies and mechanisms.
Key topics discussed included ensuring the fair and reliable use of AI, and strategies to maximize the benefits and mitigate the risks of using artificial intelligence for the benefit of all ASEAN member states.
