Mr. Pen Bona: Cambodia is the least taxed and favorable country, but the development is fast
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government led by the Cambodian People's Party since the time of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, former Prime Minister and current Prime Minister Hun Manet, has provided the most favorable tax collection from the people, especially the poor and low-income people. The Royal Government has given priority and tried to avoid them from being taxed.
In fact, the state does not tax family farmland, does not tax agricultural materials, agricultural products and real estate worth less than 100 million riels or 25,000 US dollars. Exemption from stamp duty on the transfer of ownership of immovable property under or equal to 70,000 USD.
The state does not tax stamp duty, transfer inheritance as a one-time gift, does not tax motorcycle or tricycle roads. Salary less than 1.5 million riels is not taxable. Small business owners with a turnover of less than 250 million riels are not required to pay taxes. At the same time, favorable policies for disadvantaged businesses have been put in place and are being implemented on a regular basis. There are still many concessions and exemptions provided by the state.
By: Mr. Pen Bona, Head of the Government Spokesperson Unit
