More than 70 national and international journalists attend the 3rd Mekong Journalism Training Course on "The Role of the Media in Fighting Fraud and Fake News"
(Phnom Penh): The Institute of International Relations of Cambodia of the Royal Academy of Cambodia has partnered with the Club of Cambodian Journalists to organize a workshop on "The Role of the Media in Combating False Information and Fake News in the Context of Artificial Intelligence for Peace, Stability and Regional Prosperity." This workshop was held for 2 days from 05 to 6 June 2024 at the Royal Academy of Cambodia.
The workshop was chaired by Mr. Chum Kosal, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information, represented by Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information, Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, and was attended by professors of information, civil servants and national journalists. International from some Mekong countries.
The workshop was attended by 74 journalists from Cambodia, China, Indonesia, Malaysia and the Philippines, as well as leaders, government officials, researchers of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and 24 institutions.
Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia, said that as of 2024, the Royal Academy of Cambodia has organized three workshops, including:
* The first Mekong Media Training Workshop on "The Role of the Media in Election Reporting" was held from 28 to 29 December 2022 under the chairmanship of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, former Minister of Information and current Member of the National Assembly.
* The 2nd Media Training Workshop on "Media Participation for the Mekong Region, Peace, Stability and Prosperity" was held from 26 to 28 April 2023 under the chairmanship of Dr. Sok Touch, President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia .
The third Media Training Workshop on "The Role of the Media in Combating Fraud and Fake Information in the Context of Artificial Intelligence for Peace, Stability and Regional Prosperity" is currently chaired by Secretary of State Chum Kosal. Information and Representative Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information.
Dr. Kin Phea added that in the fight against fraud, the ASEAN region has focused on digital literacy, censorship and the fight against fraud in the media. These efforts involve guidelines for government information management, the establishment of working groups and programs such as the ASEAN Digital Literacy Program, and initiatives such as the ASEAN Real Information Network.
According to Leang De Lux, Executive Director of the Club of Cambodian Journalists, the Club of Cambodian Journalists believes that the third Mekong Media Training Workshop is entitled "The Role of the Media in Combating False Information and Fake News in the Context of Artificial Intelligence for Peace". "Regional stability and prosperity is a very important forum for journalists."
The senior official of the Ministry of Information said that the fake news caused divisions in national unity, affected national security and foreign relations, led to mistrust, class division and violence among the people. In addition, fake news and fake news have undermined people's trust and confidence in the media, which has tarnished the image of the media.
