South Korea to resume all military activities along inter-Korean border
SEOUL: The South Korean military on Tuesday said it would resume military action along the border that divides the two Koreas after the complete suspension of military agreements with North Korea. This was released by Reuters on Tuesday, June 4, 2024.
Under the military agreement, the two countries agreed to completely stop all hostile activities against each other, which is a source of military tensions, such as the eruption of conflict through various measures such as The fact that both sides decided to stop military exercises near the border area. It is the clearest agreement emerging from the historic meeting between the two Korean leaders in 2018.
However, the agreement collapsed when South Korea announced the suspension of parts of the military agreement after North Korea successfully launched a military reconnaissance satellite into space last year. Soon after, Pyongyang announced that it was no longer under the terms of the agreement. Since then, North Korea has deployed troops and weapons at checkpoints near the border.
