National Bank of Cambodia launches old riel banknote exchange campaign in front of Banlung Market, Ratanakkiri Province
(Rattanakiri): The campaign to exchange old and torn banknotes was held on the morning of June 4, 2024 in the presence of Mr. Thou Khoeur, Governor of Banlung and Mr. Nhet Nuth, Branch Manager of the National Bank of Cambodia, Rattanakiri Province and Sangkat Chief. The four of Banlung City and the village chiefs in the four communes as well.
Separately, today, the National Bank of Cambodia branch in Ratanakkiri province, in cooperation with 16 banking and financial institutions, organized a campaign to exchange old riel banknotes for the public free of charge and to be transferred through bank account and Bakong account. Of the public immediately on the spot.
Mr. Nhet Nuth said that the campaign has two purposes, including:
* First, promote the use of "KHQR" payment system in the banking system more widely throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia in accordance with the policy policy, strategy, pentagon, the first phase of the Royal Government, the seventh legislature of the National Assembly, people, roads, water, electricity and digital technology. * Second: Establish Bakong account and bank account to the public free of charge at the banking and financial institution booth.
He added that the National Bank of Cambodia established the Bakong system on October 28, 2020 as a payment system to enable the public to transact easily, securely, quickly and free of charge.
To date, there are 73 members of Bakong system, 57 have been activated and 16 systems are connected, 27 million can be operated through Bakong, 0.6 million customers have registered with Bakong program and merchants can be paid through Bakong 2.9 million accounts. Bakong KHQR system is a new payment system in the new KHQR era for all.
Speaking at the opening ceremony of the campaign, Mr. Thu Khoe said that the use of the riel is very important because the riel has helped to promote national identity. The riel builds trust, promotes unity and cultivates national unity and spirit in the country.
The mayor said that in terms of the economy, more riel circulation would boost the effectiveness of monetary policy. On the other hand, the use of the riel will also help the government make a profit in issuing currency. In addition, if the riel is used in the market, the transaction value of the exchange will be reduced.
The mayor of Banlung called on the general public to join in creating a Bakong account for everyone, because the Bakong account is a payment system to enable the public to transact easily, securely, quickly and free of charge.
