The ceremony took place this morning, June 4, 2024, at the Phnom Penh Hotel, with the participation of the President, Vice President and members of the Public Administration Reform Working Group, representatives of all ministries and institutions, as well as leaders and Many professional officials involved in public administration reform.
At the opening of the training, Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many highlighted the importance of functional analysis and the importance of the Ministry of Public Function in leading the analysis of special functions to achieve the vision of the President in the Royal Government of the 7th legislature of the National Assembly.
In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many also gave six recommendations to the participants who participated in the training, including:
* First, the review, analysis, function and structure of ministries and institutions must be carried out based on the approach focused on the organization of our homes, by strengthening the structure rather than expanding the structure in accordance with the recommendations of His Majesty the King Hun Manet, Director Minister of Cambodia
* Second: Review, analysis, function and structure of ministries and institutions and update the data structure of civil servants. Ministries and institutions must be based on ownership, accountability and accountability of officials.
* Third: A clear analysis of the functions and structure of ministries and institutions to take into account the efficiency and performance of work through the use of budget resources, human resources to be more effective, targeted at the place in accordance with the roles and responsibilities of each ministry.
* Fourth: Ministries and institutions must prepare to review, analyze the functions and structure of ministries and institutions and update the data structure of civil servants to respond within the allotted time.
Mr. Chea Chandara: Prek Chik Funan-Techo will improve the transportation sector in Cambodia, provide convenience to investors who wish to invest in Cambodia
(CHITAO): At the invitation of the Asia-Pacific Logistics Federation and the China Logistics and Purchasing and Ordering Federation of China, Mr. Chea Chandara, President of the Cambodian Association of Freight Forwarders and Supply Chains, attended the Logistics Forum for Exchange. Knowledge and experience sharing among different countries, with the participation of nearly 500 people from different countries in Chitao, China.
In particular, on the same day, there was also a meeting of the Asia-Pacific Logistics Federation, where gold came from the Asia-Pacific region, including Cambodia. The meeting focused on operations between members in the region, including standard logistics and innovation.
Speaking to Fresh News on June 4, Mr. Chea Chandara said that at that time, he mentioned many developments in the field of transportation and logistics under the efforts of the Royal Government over the years. In particular, the creation of a new waterway through the digging of the Funan-Techo canal, which will improve Cambodia's transport sector, providing convenience to investors wishing to invest in Cambodia.
The Funan-Techo Canal Project is a project to connect waterways between rivers to the sea of Cambodia, passing through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces, about 180 kilometers long. The project is expected to cost about $ 1.7 billion and has been studied in detail.
It should be noted that the Asia-Pacific Logistics Federation holds two meetings a year, online and face-to-face, in which members of the federation will be hosted through shifts and requests. Chinese spacecraft rises from the moon to bring prototype back to Earth
