Pursat Provincial Governor Vows to Promote Tree Planting Movement in Talo Sen Chey District Hall to Become a Green Model District
(Pursat): Mr. Khoy Rida, Governor of Pursat Province, has vowed to promote the planting of mixed seedlings and fruit trees in accordance with the plan in the administrative area of Talo Sen Chey District Hall (newly established district) in Thlok Dangkor village, Phteah commune. Rong Talo Sen Chey district, Pursat province, to make this district a leading model district with new administrative infrastructure and beautiful greenery.
He stated that on both sides of the road, both the main road and the small road, according to the plan, peacock trees will be planted, and various mixed trees and other fruit trees will also be planted continuously to be beautiful, orderly and have a good row, especially planting. By being careful not to die.
He said that the plan to plant trees is to attract the attention of the people as well as government officials who come to receive and provide administrative services seem to feel cool and refreshed and exercise for health and to contribute to the prevention of natural disasters. Such as hurricanes, tornadoes, floods and other natural phenomena that may occur eventually.
At the same time, the Governor of Khoy Rida Province also asked the leaders and administrative officials of Talo Sen Chey District to participate in maintaining and protecting all these achievements so that the newly formed district will have green information and Beautify for the next 2 to 3 years.
It should be informed that on January 08, 2019, the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to issue a sub-decree to establish another Talo Sen Chey district in the territory of Pursat province. Talo Sen Chey district has just two communes, including Talor commune, which is cut off from Bakan district, and Phteah Rong commune, which is cut off from Phnom Kravanh district in Pursat province.
At the same time, the Royal Government also cut two villages, Koh Svay village and Koh Wat village from Khnar Toteung commune of Bakan district to Talor commune of Talo Sen Chey district. The location of the district hall is in Thlok Dangkor village, Phteah Rong commune, Talo Sen Chey district, Pursat province, while the construction of the district administration building and the OWSO has already been completed.
