During his visit, in addition to meeting with Samdech Techo and Samdech Thipadei, Mr. Loy Austin will also meet with Deputy Prime Minister Tea Seiha, Minister of National Defense of Cambodia. There will also be a formal reception at the Ministry of Defense prior to the meeting.
Loy Austin's current one-day visit to Cambodia is seen as a contribution to improving defense relations and cooperation between Cambodia and the United States.
The Ministry of National Defense of Cambodia considers this to be the first official official visit to Cambodia to continue to strengthen and expand the good cooperation between the two countries, Cambodia-US, which has been more than 70 years, especially through Promote the implementation of cooperation between the two governments.
The Department of Defense claims that the official visit of US Secretary of Defense Loy Austin will reaffirm the long-standing friendship and underscore the commitment of the United States Department of Defense and the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces to a key partnership. To deepen defense cooperation for the maintenance of peace, stability and sustainable development of the two countries, as well as for the region as a whole.
