Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many: Ministries, Institutions and Sub-National Administrations That Do Not Review the Structure and Functional Analysis Are Not Allowed to Recruit Officials
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hun Many, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Public Works and Permanent Deputy Chairman of the National Committee for Promoting the Implementation of Key Measures for Public Administration Reform of the Royal Government of the 7th Legislature of the National Assembly (CCV) affirmed. That in the case of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations that do not carry out structural review and functional analysis are not allowed to recruit civil servants.
This assertion of Deputy Prime Minister Hun Many was made this morning, May 4, 2024, on the occasion of presiding over the opening of the training course on reviewing and analyzing the functions and structure of ministries and institutions and updating the data of civil servants. Ministry of Institutions.
In addition, on behalf of the CAVR Secretariat The Ministry of Public Function shall coordinate the complete implementation of the structural review and functional analysis of ministries, institutions and sub-national administrations by the third quarter of 2024.
Mr. HUN Many emphasized that as a result of the improvement of the recruitment system for public administration, the Ministry of Public Works has developed a set of operating procedures for the civil service recruitment competition, which has been implemented through a sub-decree. The Ministry has led six civil service recruitment competitions, selecting a total of 975 candidates and is in the process of selecting them.
Please be informed that the training course on reviewing the analysis of functions and structure of ministries and institutions and updating the data structure of civil servants of ministries and institutions is another step in achieving public administration reform.
