Senior officials of the Ministry of Women's Affairs call on all service providers to fully participate in the prevention and effective response to violence against women and girls
(Preah Vihear): Ms. Hou Samith, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, instructed the trainees who participated in the training on Law and Procedures on Judicial Police and relevant service providers from 8 provinces to fully participate in prevention. And effective response to violence against women and girls.
The Deputy Governor stated that violence against women and girls is a violation of human rights that causes harm or physical, emotional and economic harm to women, including threats to commit acts. This will have a serious impact on livelihoods, human resource development, poor living conditions, loss of income to support the family.
She said that most of the victims were women and children who had been subjected to various kinds of rights violations, but the most heinous violation was the "violence against women" that resulted in The most common in our country include:
* Domestic violence * Rape * Human trafficking and sexual harassment in the workplace.
Some victims suffer from unequal power relations between men and women, and victims remain silent without seeking help from local authorities, competent authorities and other relevant service providers.
The Secretary of State said that the competent authorities and local authorities have the roles and responsibilities defined by law and also have some difficulties associated with the performance of their work.
The Capacity Development Program is a demonstration of the commitment to contribute to the better service response of all service providers and also to the third National Action Plan on the Prevention of Violence Against Women. 2019-2023 in the second strategy, legal protection and multidisciplinary services.
The overall goal of this capacity building program is for all of us as service providers to fully participate in the prevention and response to the use of violence against women and girls effectively and environmentally.
