(Phnom Penh): Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, said that the Ministry of Agriculture is preparing a draft law on agricultural production contracts, a special law to protect the interests of farmers.
"The ministry is preparing a law on agricultural production contracts. Why is a special law needed? Because we refer to the ordinary law, the civil law means that he has to pay some damages that hurt the farmer very much, now we make special laws to help protect him, but if he has a problem, we can help Solve it.
At the same time, he added that at least we need to find a solution to the problem of supply instability, because this is difficult, according to extremists, he will say not to import, but do not forget that when we Unable to supply and not to import, the affected people are all consumers.
In addition, the Minister said that what we are doing today is to maintain this price stability by balancing supply and consumption, we do not always open to import and we do not always close. Do not forget that today we have an economy that is interconnected with a clear balance and a common interest.
