Through the success of the Children's Music and Song Festival, Minister Net Pheaktra encourages the celebration of the Children's Song Festival every year and hopes that the leaders, government officials and philanthropists will continue to support this program. For the benefit of the children who are the heirs of Cambodia's bamboo in the future.
He instructed all boys and girls to strive to build themselves, study and learn to become good children, good students, good friends and good citizens, which are important resources to contribute to the development of the nation.
He also thanked all the relevant poets who have worked together for the national cause and the benefit of Cambodian children by creating works of music and lyrics for children based on easy-to-remember principles.
According to a brief report by Ms. Chanthy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Information in charge of the Scoring Committee, the Children's Music and Song Festival was established from 1985 to 2012 with the support of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, former Minister of Information. Continued support until 2019, but was suspended for almost three years due to the spread of Kovid-19 disease.
In 2024, the Children's Music and Song Festival will be held again under the initiative of Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information. The boys and girls who participated in the contest were 34 groups of songs, 68 lyrics with meaning, meaning, good taste and a message to provide comprehensive education, knowledge, covering the morals and behavior of children.
