North Korea Condemns Call for Nuclear Disarmament at Seoul Neighborhood Summit
SEOUL: North Korea on Monday condemned China, Japan and South Korea over their joint commitment to nuclear disarmament on the Korean Peninsula, describing the three countries' joint statement after a rare summit. In Seoul as a "serious political provocation" that violates its sovereignty. This is according to the release by Reuters on May 27, 2024.
North Korea announced its plans to launch a rocket in early June to launch a reconnaissance satellite that will help increase the country's nuclear capability. At the first trilateral summit in Seoul since 2019, the three countries sought security cooperation, reaffirming their positions on peace, stability and nuclear disarmament on the Korean Peninsula.
China once angered North Korea when it signed a UN Security Council resolution imposing sanctions on Pyongyang's nuclear and missile programs from 2006 to 2017, but in recent years Beijing has joined Russia in blocking new sanctions and called for the easing of existing measures.
