Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, reminded and encouraged Cambodian students studying in China to study hard and not give up their studies to develop the country.
According to the report of the President of the Association, the Cambodian Students Association of the People's Republic of China (ACSC) was established on May 11, 2017 through the recognition of the Cambodian Embassy in China and Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation with Mr. Oum Vutty as the founder of the association. The association currently has a total of 1,067 members (450 women) studying in 26 provinces of China.
As a result, the student association has successfully achieved in 37 high schools, 10 universities in Phnom Penh, Tbong Khmum, Kampong Cham, Takeo, Kampong Speu, Svay Rieng, Ratanakkiri and Kampot provinces with a total of more than 20,000 participants.
In addition, the association received support from the Office of Economy and Commerce of the Chinese Embassy in Cambodia to facilitate the recruitment of young people and students to participate in online workshops on 105 topics (2-3 weeks) with participants from The association has 138 members from May 2021 to 2023 and live seminars in China (two weeks) from June 2023 to the present, a total of 10 topics with a total of 51 participants.
In addition, the student association also participated as an international observer for the 7th National Assembly election in 2023, for the 5th legislative Senate election in 2024, and also participated as an international observer for the election. Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan, 4th mandate, 2024, recently.
