Russia's Defense Ministry has sent troops to the rescue in response to Armenia's request. The TASS news agency quoted the Armenian interior minister as saying that three people had been killed in a village along the Debed River near the border with Georgia. Hundreds of homes were flooded and 230 rescuers were dispatched to the area. In Georgia, at least 15 villages were cut off by heavy rains.
