To begin with, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure at meeting the Ambassador, but also felt sad at the end of his mission and had to leave Cambodia.
Samdech thanked the Ambassador for his contribution to the strengthening and expansion of Cambodia-China relations during his tenure as Ambassador to Cambodia for nearly six years, during which he was very busy and worked together as a Lots of great success, especially in the Kovid stage, where Samdech worked closely with him to prevent the spread of the disease.
He also conveyed greetings from President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Li Chheang to Samdech Techo. He also congratulated the CPP on its glorious success in the by-elections, especially the Senate election in February, which is a testament to the Cambodian people's trust in the CPP's leadership. .
He stressed that China and Cambodia are traditional friends and steel friends. He is most honored in his life as the Ambassador to Cambodia and has been given the opportunity to promote Sino-Cambodian relations and attend many historic events in Cambodia.
He is most pleased to have worked with the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo in the 6th legislature and under the leadership of Samdech Thep in the 7th legislature of the National Assembly, which has brought socio-economic development and well-being to the people. Cambodia. He congratulated Cambodia on the smooth transfer of power to the next generation of leaders and congratulated Samdech on his election as President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Under the Belt and Road Initiative (BRI), China and Cambodia have jointly transformed Sihanoukville into a multi-purpose model special economic zone and built a number of infrastructures, especially the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone, Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway. And Siem Reap International Airport, Morat Techo Stadium, etc. As a result of the signing of the China-Cambodia Free Trade Agreement (FTA), the trade volume between the two countries has increased significantly.
He also reminded of Cambodia's success in hosting the Asia-Europe Summit as the chair of ASEAN and the organization of the SEA Games, which has promoted Cambodia in the international arena, as well as Cambodia's success in the fight against Kovid 19 with the contribution of the country and the people of China. This is a testament to China's sympathy with Cambodia.
He thanked the King and the Royal Government of Cambodia for maintaining a fair stance on the South China Sea, the Taiwan issue and the Xinjiang region aimed at protecting the Sino-Cambodian and ASEAN-China interests. The world situation changes, Sino-Cambodian relations do not change. He said that the Chinese people will be excited to receive Samdech Techo's visit to China in the future.
Samdech Techo emphasized that the Cambodian-Chinese relationship, which is a long-standing historical relationship, has grown to an inseparable level. This relationship is worthy of the values of mutual trust, especially political trust. China's assistance to Cambodia not only helps socio-economic development, but also strengthens Cambodia's political independence.
He reiterated that despite the change of Prime Minister and Council of Ministers in Cambodia, there has been no change in the position of Cambodian relations with China and wished Cambodia-China friendship to last forever.
Regarding cooperation on prevention of Kovid 19 disease, Samdech Techo expressed his gratitude to Chinese friends for making Cambodia able to fight this disease successfully. Samdech Techo also commended the Ambassador for assisting Cambodia in the fight against Kovid 19 in the past.
Finally, Samdech Techo Senate President asked him to send a message of greetings to Chinese President Xi Jinping, Prime Minister Li Chiang and other Chinese leaders and wish him good health and continued success. Next and hope that he will return to Cambodia and be present in Cambodia in the future.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chhay Rithi Sen, Minister of Rural Development, on May 27, 2024, chaired a meeting to review the work results for May and the work direction for June 2024 of the Ministry of Rural Development.
