Anti-Corruption Unit and Guangdong Provincial State Oversight Committee Commit to Enhancing Anti-Corruption Cooperation and Exchange Information
(Phnom Penh): The Anti-Corruption Unit (ACU) and the State Inspection Committee of the Guangdong Province of the People's Republic of China have pledged to increase joint anti-corruption cooperation, especially mutual information exchange and surveillance. And detain any person who escapes from China to Cambodia or from Cambodia to China.
This commitment coincides with the visit of a delegation of the Guangdong Provincial State Inspection Committee to the Anti-Corruption Unit on the morning of May 27, 2024, with the aim of exchanging experiences and strengthening cooperation on anti-corruption work of the two countries. Two.
The Chinese delegation was led by Song Fulong, a member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Guangdong Provincial Committee, secretary of the Disciplinary Inspection Commission of the CPC Guangdong Provincial Committee and chairman of the Guangdong Provincial State Inspection Committee. Welcomed by Mr. Om Yentieng, Senior Minister, Chairman of the Anti-Corruption Unit.
Senior Minister Om Yentieng told the Chinese delegation during a visit that on April 17, 2010, the National Assembly of Cambodia passed the Anti-Corruption Law and established an anti-corruption body. Anti-corruption is based on three main principles: 1- Education by educating to hate corruption, education to love integrity and love of cleanliness, 2-Prevention and prevention, 3-Suppression and case building Go to court.
Mr. Song Fullong thanked Dr. Om Yentieng for his warm welcome and for sharing his anti-corruption experience in Cambodia with the Chinese delegation. He also invited Senior Minister Om Yentieng to visit Guangdong to further enhance cooperation in the fight against corruption.
The Anti-Corruption Unit and the Guangdong Provincial State Oversight Committee have pledged to increase joint anti-corruption cooperation, especially mutual information exchange, as well as the search, investigation and arrest of fugitives. From China to Cambodia or from Cambodia to China.
During the visit to the Anti-Corruption Unit, the Chinese delegation visited a number of locations, such as the Complaints Analysis Room, the Polygraph Room, the Operations Room, the Interrogation Room, the Suspension Room, and the Assets and Debt Collection Warehouse. .
