(Phnom Penh): The Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Department of the National Police General Commission this morning, May 27, 2024, continued to cooperate with Aeon Mall 3 in Meanchey District, Phnom Penh to launch fire and rescue drills. In addition to the professional police officers of the department, there are also many employees of Aeon Mall 3.
Brigadier General Sek Thoeun, Deputy Director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Department, said that the joint exercise is now to give professional police officers the opportunity to explain some technical work to the staff of Aeon 3 to be clear. And participate in prevention, especially first aid when a fire occurs.
Brigadier General Sek Thoeun affirmed that following the guidance of Brigadier General Sar Thet, the National Police Commissioner, especially Lt. Gen. Neth Vantha, Director of the Fire Prevention and Rescue Police Department, professional police officers always provide good cooperation with enterprises. Especially large markets to help train staff on preventive and first aid measures.
He realized that so far, Aeon Mall has always maintained close cooperation with professional departments and also regularly held joint exercises in all three branches of Aeon Mall. He considers that this is a model that other site owners should follow, especially in accordance with the legal standards in force.
At the same time, Mr. Chou Sovannara, General Manager of Aeon Mall 3, said that Aeon 3 Mall always requests the cooperation of the Police Department for Fire Prevention and Rescue so that the staff know more and be ready to prevent and rescue fires. . In addition, to make the police officers of the specialized department aware of the interlocking location of the market's plumbing network.
He added that the request for cooperation in this exercise is also to provide all market staff with more knowledge and strengthen the spirit in case of fire, easy to manage and report for intervention. He added that all Aeon Mall, especially Aeon Meanchey (Aeon 3) continue to cooperate with specialized departments to strengthen the capacity of individuals.
