The exercise is aimed at exchanging experiences, maintaining operations, increasing trust and further developing relations between the two navies.
The first "Golden Dragon-2024" naval exercise between the Cambodian and Chinese armies was held for 12 days, from May 16 to 27, with the participation of a total of 782 Cambodian-Chinese navies. In this first naval exercise, the two armies used 14 ships (Cambodia has 11 participating ships, China has 3 warships) and 2 helicopters in the operation to rescue the hostages from the kidnapped terrorists. Cargo ship.
The closing ceremony of the naval exercise will be presided over by General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff and Chairman of the Exercise and Exercise Committees with friendly countries, and Admiral Kao Siuqing, Deputy Chief of Staff of the Southern Region. Chinese People's Liberation Army gems.
The naval exercise took place in the area between Koh Tang and Koh Rong Samloem, Sihanoukville Province, from the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port, divided into three groups of ships.
According to Major General Thong Solimo, spokesman for the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), the exercise will pave the way for better cooperation between the two armies, especially the exchange of experience, capacity building on the use of force. The Navy, in tackling the challenges, contributes to the cause of regional peacekeeping.
Separately, as planned, the Cambodian-Chinese Army will hold the closing ceremony of the Neak Meas Naval Exercise 2024 together under the theme "Operation to release hostages from terrorists hijacking cargo ships" on May 27, 2024. On the waters of Cambodia.
2024 is the first year that the Royal Cambodian Navy and the Chinese People's Liberation Army have joined forces to conduct the Golden Dragon Exercise, to exchange experiences, maintain close cooperation, build stronger trust and continue to develop relations. Between the two countries, Cambodia and China to improve to another level and jointly face challenges as well as contribute more importantly to the cause of maintaining peace in the region.
Please be informed that in 2024, this is the year of the sixth joint Golden Dragon exercise between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army, more than 2,000 people, accompanied by 14 warships and other military equipment participated in the exercise. Golden Dragon "under the theme" Joint counter-terrorism operations and humanitarian work. " The 6th Golden Dragon Exercise will be held for 14 days from 16 to 30 May 2024.
The 6th Golden Dragon Exercise between the two armies is larger than the previous ones due to the large number of participating troops, as well as expanding the level of surface exercises, with both sides using up to 14 warships. Original.
The content of the exercise is focused on counter-terrorism and humanitarian work, in addition to focusing on drone countermeasures. The exercise also invited ASEAN countries to observe the nature of the exercise between the two armies.
The 6th Golden Dragon Exercise 2024 between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army on Cambodian territory is not intended to threaten or harm any country. Cambodia always welcomes friendly countries that wish to conduct exercises but must respect Cambodia's rights.
