(Preah Vihear): Two suspects were arrested by the police force of Kulen District Police Inspectorate of Preah Vihear Province after stabbing a victim who was traveling on the road with a spare sword.
Colonel O Seng, Kulen District Police Inspector, said this morning, May 26, 2024, that the arrest of the two gangsters, the new administrative police station, has received complaints from residents that there was an attempted murder. Two men on two motorbikes stopped the road for questioning and were holding a spare sword to stab the victim in Damnak Kantuot village, Thmey commune, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province at 13:35 on May 24, 2024.
After receiving the complaint and the order, Major General Suos Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner for Criminal Affairs, cooperated with the new administrative police station to open an investigation and identify and arrest the two suspects, including: 1. Smin Rinphet Male, 44 years old, Occupation: Farmer 2. Name: Khan Chet, Male, 24 years old, Both live in Kulen Tbong village, Kulen Tbong commune, Kulen district, Preah Vihear province.
In front of the police, the two suspects confessed that they actually chased the victim on a motorcycle and removed the sword, acting as alleged, and then left the sword at home. After the suspect confessed, the police asked for a search of the suspect's house and found nine knives and swords, smoking tools, drugs and some packaging materials.
Currently, these two targets have been sent by the Kulen District Police Inspectorate to the Preah Vihear Provincial Police for further action in accordance with legal procedures.
