Today, Cambodia is preparing for the 4th Mandate Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council Election, 5 Political Parties Participate in this Election
(Phnom Penh): On May 26, 2024, Cambodia will hold the election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council of the fourth mandate. Five political parties are participating in this election.
From 2009 to 2024, Cambodia has already passed the election of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils for 3 terms, while in 2024, Cambodia will hold the 4th Mandate Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council elections. Every 5 years, the constituency is a member of the Commune / Sangkat Council.
Let's know about the election process of Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council in each mandate as follows:
* Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council Election Event of the first mandate started in 2009, when there were 24 provincial capitals, 194 municipalities, districts, Khans, including 374 members of Capital, Provincial Councils and 2 District, District and Khan Councilors. There were 850 registered voters, 11,353, and 11,349 registered voters, representing 99.96 percent of the registered voters.
In the first round of Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council elections, four political parties competed, including:
First: the Cambodian People's Party won 2,566 seats, second: the Sam Rainsy Party won 583 seats, third: FUNCINPEC won 61 seats and fourth: Norodom Rith Party won 44 seats.
* Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council Election Event of the second mandate was held in 2014. At that time, there were 25 capitals, provinces, 197 municipalities, districts, Khans, including 393 members of the Capital, Provincial Councils, and District, District and Khan Councilors. There were 2,931 registered voters, 11,459, and 11,456 registered voters, representing 99.97 percent of the registered voters.
In the Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council elections of the second mandate, 5 political parties competed, but only 4 political parties won seats, including:
First: the CPP won 2,540 seats, second: the CNRP won 765 seats, third: FUNCINPEC won 18 seats and fourth: the Alliance for Democracy won 1 seat.
* Capital, Province, Municipality, District and Khan Council Election Event of the 3rd Mandate was held in 2019. At that time, there were 25 Capital, Province, 203 Municipalities, Districts, Khans, including 559 Capital, Provincial and District Councilors and Khan / Khan Councilors. There were 3,555 registered voters, 11,572 and 11,565 registered voters, representing 99.94% of the registered voters.
In the 3rd Mandate Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Council Elections, 7 political parties competed, but only 3 parties won seats, including:
