The King of Cambodia is the Supreme King at the Royal Plowing Ceremony in Kampong Speu Province
(Kampong Speu): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, on the morning of May 26, 2024, presided over the Royal Plowing Ceremony at Preah Sre in the Department of Education. Youth and Sports is located in Chbar Morn City, Kampong Speu Province.
In this royal ceremony, Mr. Vy Samnang, Governor of Kampong Speu Province, was assigned as the King of Heaven to celebrate the plowing in the field in front of Preah Ponlea Chey. According to the royal tradition of royal ceremonies since ancient times.
The Royal Plowing Ceremony is held for the purpose of seeing the omens of the district and the cultivation according to the eating of the royal cows. This ceremony is also a reminder to the Cambodian people who rely mainly on agriculture to know that the rainy season, the season of farming has arrived.
After the plowing ceremony is over, the royal oxen are no longer allowed to eat seven pre-prepared foods: rice, corn, sesame seeds, beans, wine, water and grass. In fact, Usapreach cows ate only three notable varieties, consisting of 95% rice, 95% corn and 85% soybeans, which is predicted that the cultivation of rice, corn and soybeans this year, the year 2024, will have good results, high yields up to To 95%.
Afterwards, His Majesty the King of the Kingdom of Cambodia visited the exhibition of agricultural products, agriculture, industry and handicrafts in the exhibition during the Royal Plowing Festival.
