The Royal Plowing Ceremony is held every year in the month of Pisak, one of the main ceremonies of the Golden Gate Festival. This traditional royal ceremony is held in order to see the omens of the country according to the eating of "Usapreach" on 7 foods, including: rice, beans, corn, sesame, grass, water and wine. Moreover, this royal ceremony is also a reminder to the Cambodian people who rely mainly on agriculture to know that the rainy season has arrived.
