Here is some history of the Royal Plowing Ceremony:
The Royal Plowing Ceremony, held annually in the month of Pisak, is one of the most important royal ceremonies after the royal wedding, and is one of many royal ceremonies. Annually classified as the Royal Golden Gate Ceremony. In ancient India and in the Kingdom of Cambodia, agriculture was the main occupation, relying entirely on rice and other crops.
In fact, the creation of rice or other crops such as corn, beans, sesame by the king through the above ceremony is due to one of the main factors is the sanctity of the character "king" in the eyes of the people. This means that the crop is not just about cultivation, technique or economy, that is, due to the ritual itself.
