Understand the important role of Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils
(Phnom Penh): On May 26, 2024, tomorrow, Cambodia will hold the election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council of the fourth mandate. Five political parties are participating in this election.
The election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council and Khan Council shall be held non-universal, free, fair and just by secret ballot. These eligible voters are not ordinary citizens, but commune councilors elected by the people within the mandate.
The council may exercise its executive power by making decisions at council meetings. The council must be directly accountable to all citizens for priority choices in making decisions to ensure democratic development within its jurisdiction.
The council shall prepare and approve a five (5) year development plan, which shall be updated annually in accordance with the annual three (3) year rolling investment program. In preparing and implementing the development plan, the council shall consult with: * Citizens within its jurisdiction * Other types of councils within its jurisdiction * Ministries, institutions and relevant units of the Royal Government * Stakeholders .
The council shall approve the budget of the sub-national administration in accordance with the procedures and calendar of the annual state budget. The council must approve the medium-term expenditure framework and update it annually.
