Bassac River Navigation and Logistics System Project "Prek Chik Funan Techo" connects the river between the river to the sea of Cambodia through Kandal, Takeo, Kampot and Kep provinces with a length of 180 billion US dollars. America.
The Funan Techo Canal will connect the Phnom Penh Autonomous Port to the deep-water port under construction in Kep and the completed deep-sea port in Sihanoukville. Currently, a large part of Cambodia's trade, especially in and out of Phnom Penh, is conducted through the southern ports of Vietnam, such as Cai Mep.
The Cambodian government has calculated in detail that the Funan Techo canal will reduce dependence on Vietnamese ports by up to 70 percent. At present, Cambodia's ports are not very commercial and do not collect much tax.
