Separately, a man named Sokea, a broker who buys mushrooms, said that in relation to the price of mushrooms, the price is higher or lower than the first time, meaning that in some areas there are no mushrooms, so the area. There are mushrooms bought by traders at a high price, but now there are mushrooms in all areas, which makes the price of mushrooms fall.
The broker stated that whether the price of mushrooms went up or down for him as a broker, it was still a small profit, even though the price he raised from the people who sold to the exporters made a profit of 1,000 riel to 1,500 riel, especially when the price dropped. He still makes a profit, but in a day he can collect 400 to 500 kilos of mushrooms from the people to sell to traders see that the profit is quite a lot.
