The King Congratulates Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin on the Occasion of His 90th Birthday
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, sends a message of congratulations to Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President of the King's Supreme Council of the Kingdom of Cambodia on the occasion of prosperity. He turned 90 years old on May 25, 2024.
The King's message reads as follows: "Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei is the most esteemed and deeply loved person on the occasion of the grand anniversary of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei on May 25, In 2024, I would like to extend my best wishes to Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei, and wish him new success in fulfilling his noble mission to the motherland and the people of Cambodia.
I would like to congratulate you for your excellent work and express your sincere appreciation for the efforts of Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei, who is a great patriot who has contributed to leading the defense, building, serving the nation and the people. The people of Cambodia, in the cause of the nation, religion, and the King, make the motherland of Cambodia enjoy peace, social stability, and national development in all fields.
I would like to bless Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei and Samdech Thammavisut Vongsa, as well as his family, and wish the Buddha the best of luck, age, class, happiness, and strength. Mr. Sun Chanthol: Asia must unite to build a future and sustainable development
(Tokyo, Japan): Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, said that Asian countries must unite and work together to build a future and sustainable development.
This large annual forum has about 350 live participants and about 2,500 online participants.
In his keynote address, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol highlighted some of the current global challenges, including geopolitical changes, economic issues and global stability, holding major elections in 2024. The war in Ukraine, the Middle East and the chronic wars of Sudan, Syria and Burma.
In response to these issues, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol said that the unity of the leaders of Asian countries with a population of more than half of the world's population is very important. The participation of Asian countries will improve the situation in the world by not only defending its interests but addressing global issues to promote peace, prosperity and international cooperation.
The Deputy Prime Minister highlighted Cambodia's efforts and strong cooperation to contribute to solving these global problems. Under the high leadership of Samdech Hun Sen, the Royal Government of Cambodia has cooperated and provided solutions to common challenges more effectively and created more new opportunities for joint growth and progress as opposed to shortcomings. Collaboration.
With the long-term strategic vision of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia has many priority tasks, the main tasks of which are to focus on sustainable economic development and sustainable economic growth, which creates opportunities for All people, especially people in remote rural areas and communities where resources are limited.
The Deputy Prime Minister also highlighted the experience that Cambodia can share with the world is the importance of setting environment policies that are important for the growth and development of each nation. Thorough thinking and leaving no one will give results that increase the potential of human resources, reduce inequality and strengthen social stability. These factors are a solid foundation for national stability and progress.
Asia, with its rich, vibrant economy and aging culture, stands as a pillar of resilience and adaptive skills, relying on a concerted effort to provide innovative solutions to the challenges at hand. Global and strengthen the building of a sustainable and environmentally friendly future.
