(Kratie): Two men were involved in a case of involuntary manslaughter by trapping wild animals, causing an electric shock last weekend. Authorities are now searching for and detaining one suspect and the other escaped.
According to the police, the suspect, Neou Thuon, 49, a farmer living in Tuol Treang, O'Kreang village, O'Kreang Senchey district, Kratie province, was searched and arrested by the O'Kreang Senchey district police in cooperation with the criminal police force of the provincial police. Another suspect, Long Sun, 48, who lives in the same commune, is fleeing.
Mr. Bun Lok, the father of the victim, described that on the night of the incident, his son was walking to see the frog with his younger brother, along with two other villagers, and was electrocuted by a wild boar trap. Caused sudden death at O Trapeang Svay, Kbal Damrey commune, O Kreang Sen Chey district, Kratie province on the night of May 18, 2024.
After the incident, the victim's family reported to the village guards and the village chief and then reported to the local police force, in which the relevant professional forces of the provincial police commission visited the location where the wildlife electric shock was deployed. At the scene, the police also collected the electric wire and equipment to search for the perpetrators.
According to the police, the victim, Sen Sore, 26 years old, farmer, resided in O'Kreang village, O'Kreang commune, O'Kreang Sen Chey district, Kratie province. Authorities said that after the expert force examined the body at the scene and searched until the arrest of the suspect named Neou Thuon. He confessed that he and his brother-in-law, Long Sun, went to trap wild animals, causing the death of Sen Sore, also known as Ya.
The suspect, Neou Thuon, is currently being held in custody at the O'Kreang Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate to build a case to be sent to the provincial specialized office according to the procedure, while the suspect named Long Sun, the specialized force is still investigating.
