The meeting also focused on discussions on the contribution of the transport sector in environmental sustainability and the impact on climate, health and political geography. It is noteworthy that all member countries recognize that road safety is an important topic and the governments of all countries are working together to reduce the accident rate in the country to a maximum.
As a result, the meeting discussed and approved the following important documents: Report of the 15th Meeting of the Council of Transport Ministers of the International Transport Forum, Application for ITF membership of three countries: Dominican Republic, Oman and Saudi Arabia, The decision of the Czech Republic on the rotating chairmanship for 2026-2027 and the date of the 2025 Summit of the International Transport Forum are set for May 21-23, 2025.
