ASEAN Secretary-General meets Japanese leaders, meets Japanese media and attends Nike Forum
On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General thanked the Japanese business presence in ASEAN and invited more Japanese companies to expand their business and investment in all ASEAN member countries to explore the full potential that the region has.
On Thursday afternoon, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also met with Japanese Foreign Minister Kamikawa Yoko. On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on ASEAN-Japan relations and explored ways to further promote the ASEAN-Japan Comprehensive Strategic Partnership, which is important, meaningful and mutually beneficial.
The two sides also agreed to work closely together to promote ASEAN-Japan cooperation in line with the Declaration on the Vision of Friendship and Cooperation between ASEAN and Japan and the Implementation Plan adopted at the 50th Anniversary Summit. Of ASEAN-Japan Friendship and Cooperation in December 2023 in Tokyo.
On the same Thursday afternoon, the ASEAN Secretary-General gave an interview to TV Tokyo. On that occasion, the ASEAN Secretary-General provided insights on how ASEAN and Japan can work together to achieve carbon neutrality.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn also shared his views on the great opportunities for the people of ASEAN and Japan through efforts to strengthen existing cooperation and explore new areas of cooperation within the framework of the strategic partnership. All corners of ASEAN-Japan.
In particular, on Thursday evening, Dr. Kao Kim Hourn, Secretary-General of ASEAN, attended the 29th Nike Forum on the Future of Asia and spoke on "Digital Cross-Border Integration: Strengthening Asia-Pacific Cooperation."
The ASEAN Secretary-General stressed that digital technology has become a new driving force for ASEAN for innovation, production and economic growth, and stressed that the ASEAN Digital Economic Framework Agreement (DEFA), which will end in 2025, aims to increase the participation of the digital economy. Double to $ 2 trillion by 2030
He also highlighted ASEAN's commitment to promoting digital connectivity and digital environment initiatives to address the digital gap in ASEAN, and highlighted the importance of cyber security cooperation in ASEAN. Among ASEAN member countries, more important than ever, to make ASEAN resilient to cyber threats and attacks.
