(Kandal): Kandal Provincial Court has issued a detention order for the perpetrator of the murder of a female creditor and imprisoned him on May 23, 2024 after the prosecutor's office charged him.
Deputy Prosecutor Theam Chan Pilikar has decided to charge Long Chheav alias Cheang Lay, 32, with murder under Article 199 of the Penal Code, and Investigating Judge Art Chantara has remanded him in custody. This is according to Mr. So Sarin, Spokesman of Kandal Provincial Court and Mr. Kha Denna, Spokesman of Kandal Provincial Court, confirmed to Fresh News reporters in Kandal province on the evening of May 23, 2024.
Please be informed that this case of killing happened on May 19, 2024 at 17:35 at the house of the suspect named Long Chheav in Po Leu village, Troeuy Sla commune, Saang district, Kandal province, occupation: blacksmith.
After committing the murder, he escaped. The victim was Han Mi, a 33-year-old Cambodian female farmer living in Po Leu village, Troeuy Sla commune, Saang district, Kandal province. The woman died instantly.
The perpetrator was arrested by the police force of Kandal Provincial Police in cooperation with Veal Veng District Police Force, Pursat Province on May 21, 2024.
