Many young people are interested in the day "Vesak Bochea", a major festival in Buddhism, which Cambodia considers a national holiday.
Due to the fact that Cambodia is a Buddhist country, Cambodians consider "Vesak Bochea" to be an important festival and encourage the participation of many people, young and old.
However, it is observed that from year to year, young Cambodians seem to be more interested in other festivals in Buddhism. In fact, the "Vesak Festival" held at pagodas in Phnom Penh and other provinces was attended by a large number of young people. In fact, at Wat Nikrothavorn called "Wat Kol Toteung", it was observed that many young people attended the festival despite the rain.
Ms. Tith Chhopump added that listening to the Dharma and performing rituals at the pagoda made people feel clear, happy and calm, and it is a belief that the Khmer ancestors left behind both ancient times. She observes that most young people are now more interested in Buddhism than foreign religions. She also suggested that young people unite to spread our Buddhism rather than propagate their religion.
From year to year, young Cambodians are more interested in Buddhist festivals, which is different from the past to attend festivals in the presence of only the elderly. This is according to the grandmother who prayed at the pagoda at Koul Toteung pagoda for 10 years.
She expressed her happiness that young Cambodians now understand and participate in Buddhist festivals to jointly spread Buddhism, the state religion. Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth: In the last 10 years, the increase in health expenditure in Cambodia has almost tripled from $ 226 million in 2013 to $ 573 million in 2023
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Council for Social Protection, has stated that in the last 10 years, health expenditures in Cambodia have increased by approximately $ 573 million. Nearly 3 times.
This statement was made on the occasion of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth's participation in the launching ceremony of the "Roadmap to Global Health Coverage in Cambodia" under the presidency of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia today. May 23, 2024.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, the Royal Government's investment in the health sector over the last three decades has been substantial and has brought with it many proud achievements.
At the same time, Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth said that as a trend, spending in this sector will continue to increase further, linked to strengthening efficiency and cost efficiency as well as improving the health outcomes of the people.
Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth said that through past investment in the health sector, a number of indicators have clearly reflected the progress of the road to global health coverage, including:
At the same time, the components of the social health protection system, including: the Health Equity Fund and the social security system for health care, have been implemented and expanded. This is the additional confirmation of Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth.
China warns Taiwanese independence group as new Taiwanese leader vows to protect freedom and democracy
BEIJING (Reuters) - The Chinese government on Thursday issued a stern warning to those who support Taiwan's independence, stressing that military exercises around Taiwan are aimed at sending a "serious warning message." This was released by the AFP news agency on Thursday, May 23, 2024.
Beijing considers Taiwan an inseparable part of its territory and has vowed to reunite with Taiwan one day, even using military force if necessary.
Cambodian Foreign Minister begins official visit to China and Turkey and will continue to attend the Francophone Entrepreneurship Meeting in Morocco
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia, left Cambodia on May 23, 2023 for an official visit to China and the Republic of Turkey.
The visit to the two major countries will take place from May 24 to 29, after which the Cambodian diplomat will continue to attend the 4th Francophone Entrepreneurship Meeting in Marrakesh, Morocco from 30 to 31. This coming May.
The visit is at the invitation of the Chinese and Turkish foreign ministers, and the invitation to attend the 4th Francophone Entrepreneurship Meeting is at the invitation of Jakib Al, chairman of the General Confederation of Moroccan Enterprises and Zhefai. Rhodes Bessie, President of the Francophone Employers' Alliance.
The Foreign Ministry added that during his stay in Turkey, the Deputy Prime Minister will also meet with the Cambodian community and students. The visit will be a clear testament to the strong and cordial ties that will enhance the development of relations between the two countries as Cambodia and Turkey are celebrating the 65th anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations in 2024.
After concluding his visits to China and Turkey, the Cambodian diplomat will travel to Morocco from May 30 to 31 to address the opening plenary session of the 4th Francophone Entrepreneurship Meeting. "Strengthening the Competitiveness and Resilience of Francophone Enterprises: What kind of government support is expected?" With the participation of dignitaries in the public and private sectors.
In Morocco, the Deputy Prime Minister will meet with Ms. Lewis Musiki Wabo, Secretary-General of the International Organization for Francophone (OIF) to discuss strengthening cooperation between Cambodia and the OIF, especially Cambodia's candidacy to host the Francophone Summit. 20th in 2026.
