Kampong Thom MPs Preside Over National Remembrance Day on May 20 in Prasat Sambo District
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Kheng Nupheap, Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom Constituency, in the morning of May 23, 2024, presided over the Remembrance Day Ceremony at Wat Serey Mongkul, also known as Wat Kampong Java, with the participation of Mr. Khuon Sovann, Advisor to Samdech Preah Sangkareach Bor Kry, civil servants, people and students in Kampong Java village, Koul commune, Prasat Sambo district, Kampong Thom province.
On that occasion, Mr. Kheng Noupheap said that the National Day of Remembrance on May 20 is a day that every Cambodian will remember and will never forget the genocidal regime of Pol Pot 3 years, 8 months and 20 days. The "National Day of Remembrance" is commemorated to commemorate the more than 3 million victims who lost their lives and suffered the tragic atrocities committed by the genocidal regime.
Mr. Kheng Noupheap stated that May 20, 1973 was the day the Khmer Rouge openly declared their policy to lead their country, the Great Great Leap Forward, including the evacuation of people from the city. The complete abolition of the free market economy, the abolition of the currency, the abolition of religion, the establishment of cooperatives, the eating and drinking together throughout the country, and so on.
SEOUL: The leaders of South Korea, China and Japan will hold their first summit in more than four years in Seoul from May 26 to 27, the South Korean presidential office announced on Thursday. Coming next May. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, May 23, 2024.
The three neighbors agreed to hold annual meetings starting in 2008 to boost regional cooperation, but the initiative was put on hold due to bilateral issues and Kovid 19. Their last tripartite summit was held in late 2019.
