Minister of Education inspects the implementation of model school standards at Hun Sen Throne High School, Stung Sen City, Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): On May 23, 2024, Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, led a working group to inspect the implementation of standard schools at Hun Sen Throne High School.
On this occasion, the Deputy Prime Minister praised the leadership of the school management and the teaching and learning of teachers, although the 2023 high school diploma exam did not have A-level students, but the percentage of students who passed the exam. Remarkably high.
The Deputy Prime Minister further stated that the achievement of the model school standard requires the participation of four factors, including:
* First: school factor * Second: teacher factor * Third: student factor * Fourth: parent, community guardian
The Deputy Prime Minister emphasized that in order to become a model school, five standards must be followed, including:
The Department of Secondary Education and the Department shall prepare and provide summary lessons that the Ministry has produced in the past to schools and teachers to supplement the 12th grade students using the content of these summary lessons. The results of the standardized test should be widely disseminated, especially to parents and guardians, and encourage them to continue to support supplementation and make it easier for their children to self-study on a regular basis.
* Standard 2: Teaching and learning at the secondary level, teachers need to apply new teaching methods, encourage self-study students to practice extracurricular activities, establish youth councils, establish and operate club learning and learning and teaching throughout the day. And so on.
Standard 4: School operations and administration in the sense of providing schools with physical infrastructure, promoting digital education, ensuring the implementation of health education programs, physical education and sports, arts education and other activities.
Standard 5: School accountability is enhanced by community ownership and support of the education system. The Department of Education, Youth and Sports must establish a mechanism to establish a working group and plan to assist schools on a regular basis, focusing on key activities that lead to achieving the indicators of the standard school standards.
