Mine Authority Conducts a Meeting on the Situation of Mine Action in Cambodia Towards a Cambodia Impacted by Mines and Explosive Remnants of War
(Phnom Penh): On May 23, 2024, at the Office of the Mine Authority, Dr. Ly Thuch, Senior Minister and First Vice President of the Mine Authority, chaired a meeting on the current situation of mine action in Cambodia towards a landmine-free Cambodia. Explosive Remnants of War The meeting was attended by representatives of relevant ministries and institutions, the Provincial Mine Action Committee (PMAC) and the Mine Action Planning Team (Mapu).
The Royal Government will continue its efforts to clear landmines and UXO from the war and address the long-term effects of landmines / UXO, including victim relief, assistance to affected people and communities. Displacement and socio-economic rehabilitation in areas that have been threatened by landmines / explosive remnants of war.
The Senior Minister urged the relevant ministries and institutions and sub-national administrations to continue to implement the President's high-level recommendations on the commitment and efforts to continue clearing mines and explosive remnants of war to ensure the safety of the people and contribute. National development.
On behalf of Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, Prime Minister and Chairman of the Mine Action Authority, the Senior Minister thanked the relevant ministries and institutions for always disseminating the Royal Government's efforts and achievements in resolving landmines and explosive remnants of war, as well as Take care of and consider demining as one of its priorities.
At the same time, the Senior Minister highly appreciated the Capital-Provincial Administration, which always provides guidance, cooperation and coordination of mine activities in their geographical areas to facilitate and promote the successful demining / demining. Cambodia, India and Wildlife Alliance Hold Joint Press Conference on Wildlife Management and Tiger Conservation Strategies in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Representatives of the Ministry of Environment of Cambodia, representatives of the Government of India and Wildlife Alliance on the afternoon of May 23, 2024, held a joint press conference on wildlife management and strategies to restore big tigers in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Dr. Sou Vanna Gonlet expressed her strong hope that four big tigers or leopards imported from India will be transported to live in the Cardamom Mountains of Cambodia in 2024.
According to Dr. Sou Vanna, the big tigers planned to be brought to Cambodia next year are one male and three females.
Dr. Sou Vanna Gonlet said that the Wildlife Alliance and the Ministry of Environment have installed 410 cameras throughout the Cardamom Mountains to study the exact distribution of tiger-fed wildlife. These four big tigers will be released in the core area of the Cardamom Mountains, which is protected and considered the safest way to rehabilitate big tigers in Cambodia.
The founder and executive director of the Wildlife Alliance said: "Our organization directly protects the 1.7 million hectares of rainforest in the Cardamom Mountains. We aim to protect and conserve the latest untouched rainforests in Southeast Asia. Forests, wildlife and humans can live together in harmony. "We have to work hard to achieve this."
It should be noted that on November 12, 2022, Cambodia and India signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation in Biodiversity Conservation, Sustainable Wildlife Management and Strategies to Restore Big Tigers and Their Habitats in Cambodia. Cambodia.
The Big Tiger Rehabilitation Project was established after disappearing from Cambodia in 2007, while around the world it is estimated that there were still about 3,200 big tigers in 2010. This number is 95% lower than it was in the early 20s, when there were about 100,000 in the world.
For this project to restore the big tiger after disappearing from the territory of Cambodia in 2007 by hunting for trade in bones and skins. Its presence has been found in areas such as northeast, southwest and northern Cambodia.
Japan announces development of Sihanoukville port to become regional port
This announcement was made at the request of Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol, First Vice President of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, in a meeting this morning, Thursday, May 23, 2024.
Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol is representing Cambodian Prime Minister Hun Manet at the 29th International Conference on "The Future of Asia" in Tokyo, Japan.
Taking the opportunity to attend the above international conference, the Deputy Prime Minister met with Mr. Saito TETSUO. During the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Sun Chanthol thanked the Japanese friends for their active participation in building Cambodia's socio-economic situation and building infrastructure in Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister continued that at the beginning of the seventh mandate, the Royal Government inaugurated and opened a series of infrastructure projects with the help of Japanese friends, including National Road No. 5, Choeung Ek wastewater treatment system and the project to open the construction site to improve the port of Preah Krong. Sihanouk Phase 2, Phase 1.
The Deputy Prime Minister also requested Japan to expedite the implementation of the Sihanoukville Port Promotion Project in a timely manner and to promote the study project to make Sihanoukville Port a regional port and logistics center by 2050 to boost Cambodia's economic growth. .
Minister Saito TETSUO expressed his strong commitment to urge the relevant parties to expedite the implementation of the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port Promotion Project as soon as possible to ensure that the project can be completed as planned.
In addition, the Minister also expressed his commitment to request the relevant parties to review the proposal of the master plan study project to make Sihanoukville Port a regional port and logistics center by 2050 as soon as possible to enable the study of the project. This could start soon. Pepper price increased to 20,000 riel per kilogram
(Phnom Penh): The price of pepper, which last year dropped to around 13,000 riel per kilogram, this year jumped to about 20,000 riel per kilogram, which is a remarkably high price. This is according to the president of the Cambodian Pepper and Spice Federation and pepper farmers.
He said that China is a big market where he expects that Cambodia will be able to export a lot of ordinary pepper to China, and if there are more markets and buyers, in the future, Cambodian pepper will not expect only one Vietnamese market. Cambodia can expect to export to China, including existing markets such as Europe and the United States.
Although the price of pepper this year has risen to 20,000 riel per kilogram, it has not made farmers happy. Unhappy with this year's output falling by almost two-thirds.
"The price has gone up a little bit, but we are still losing money because the costs are the same, like the cost of irrigation, fertilizer and labor," he said.
Pepper is usually harvested between March and June.
According to a report by the Ministry of Agriculture in 2023, Cambodia exported more than 6,000 tons of pepper, down nearly 27 percent compared to the same period in 2022. When driving to the railway, be careful! Train hits car in Sangkat Snour, Khan Kambol Samnang, no one was injured
(Phnom Penh): Another case! Please drive with caution when you see a railway crossing, on the morning of May 23, 2024, a train collided with a Toyota Camry Shark at the railway crossing the Phnom Penh-Battambang line in Sak Prayuth village, Snor commune. Khan Kambol, Phnom Penh, but luckily the driver was not injured.
The man said that before the incident, he was driving in the direction from east to west, when approaching the railway, he did not see the train and the train did not have a horn, so he did not stop, just As soon as he crossed the railway, the train hit his car completely, causing damage.
Residents said that at the crossing, there were only "STOP" signs, no barricades or traffic guards when there was a train crossing.
In the past, when approaching the place, the train always honked loudly again and again as a signal to warn the general public to be careful or stop, but on the day of the accident, the train did not honk at all, so there was an accident.
After the incident, the car owner asked to be free and take his car to be repaired by himself. However, the train side refused and asked the police to bring the car to be stored at the Kambol district police inspector, waiting for a solution later.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells Chinese officials that Cambodia has changed its prime minister but has not changed its position (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Senate, asked China to view Cambodia as a trustworthy friend That Cambodia has not changed its position on relations, despite the change of Prime Minister.
In this meeting, Mr. Sorat Zakir recalled the relationship between Cambodia and China and emphasized that China considers Samdech Techo a good old friend.
Mr. Sorat Zakir also announced China's position that China is committed to cooperating with Cambodia to modernize and closely cooperate to protect the sovereignty and security of the two countries. The Chinese side will also strive to deepen, modernize, innovate and share experiences with Cambodia in all fields.
Mr. Sorat Zakir also stressed that the Chinese side will promote trade cooperation, promote the import of agricultural products from Cambodia, promote the development of fish and rice corridors, industrial and technological corridors, and cooperation in road modernization. Railways, electricity, wastewater treatment, etc.
In addition, China will also promote people-to-people exchanges, as this is a year set by the two countries to boost tourism. China will also strengthen cooperation in the fight against transnational crime, online gambling, human trafficking and the dissemination of positive information.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked China for its commitment to strengthen cooperation, especially to promote cooperation in industrial and technological corridors, fish and rice corridors, etc. Samdech Techo emphasized that all this cooperation has provided many benefits to Cambodia.
Regarding the relationship between Cambodia and China, Samdech Techo asked China to look at Cambodia as a trustworthy friend and China must accept a fact from the change of the new Prime Minister, but Cambodia has not changed its position in relations with China. That no.
"The new Royal Government under the leadership of Samdech Hun Manet is working to strengthen the existing relationship with new ideas to make the relationship stronger and deeper." This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and was published on Samdech's social media.
Regarding cooperation on prevention of Kovid 19 disease, Samdech Techo thanked Chinese friends for helping Cambodia to successfully fight against this disease. Samdech Techo continued that the cooperation against Kovid 19 is very important for Cambodia-China cooperation.
Samdech Techo also commended the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia, Wang Vinthean, for assisting Cambodia in the fight against the 19-year-old Kovid. Samdech Techo considered that China's assistance not only helped to develop the economic sector, but also strengthened Cambodia's political independence.
Samdech Techo Senate President Sorat Zakir has sent a message to Chinese President Xi Jinping and other Chinese leaders and wished them good health and continued success.
In this meeting, Mr. Sorat Zakir invited Samdech Techo Hun Sen to visit China at any convenient time in the future. Mr. Sorat Zakir hopes that the cooperation between Cambodia and China will be further strengthened and enhanced. Norway bans Russian tourists
(Norway) - The Norwegian Ministry of Justice announced on Thursday that Norway will increase restrictions on Russian tourists due to the ongoing war in Ukraine through a total ban. This is according to the release by Reuters on Thursday, May 23, 2024.
Norway, a member of NATO and bordering Russia in the 200-kilometer Arctic, is the first country to have a visa ban on Russian tourists since 2022.
