(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 23, 2024, Lt. Gen. Koeng Khorn, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, represented by General Sar Thet, Commissioner of the National Police, chaired a meeting to disseminate the decision on the composition of the research and investigation mission. Violate natural resources and prevent encroachment on state land at the Ministry of Interior.
In the decision to adjust the composition of the mission to research, investigate, prevent, suppress natural resource crimes and prevent encroachment on state land, with Lt. Gen. Koeng Khorn, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police as the chairman and vice chairman, as well as some members.
On that occasion, Lt. Gen. Koeng Khorn highlighted the tasks to be performed as follows:
* Develop a practical plan and prepare operational mechanisms in accordance with the defined geographical situation
* Cooperate with relevant ministries, institutions, competent units and the Capital-Provincial Board of Governors to investigate and investigate suspected activities, natural resource crimes and encroachment on state land in order to take timely measures to prevent and suppress
Strengthen patrols at border checkpoints, informal checkpoints, and crack down on anarchic activities such as deforestation, timber transportation, and non-timber forest products, wildlife capture, wildlife export, and encroachment on state land. And illegal mining across the country
Assign, research, investigate and collect information on images, activities, sources, locations with problems, activities, activities, destruction of natural resources, for the owner to put in place effective and timely prevention and suppression measures.
* Build good people, provide information on timber storage, timber transportation, timber export, capture, wildlife export, illegal mining and encroachment on state land
* Investigate and identify the masterminds and networks who conspire to commit natural resource crimes and launch operations to arrest the perpetrators, collect evidence and build a case to be sent to court according to the procedure.
* Cooperate with Vietnam, Laos and Thailand to discuss and support the effective prevention and suppression of natural resource crimes.
* Report to the General Commission of the National Police and the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes on a regular basis in order to request timely guidance in performing other tasks assigned by the General Commission of the National Police.
He added that the mission has the right to use the officers and means of the department under its command, and the intervention force and the mainland border police battalion of the relevant provincial police commission and the deputy chairman, members of the mission must attend the meeting at the invitation of the chairman.
The head of the Natural Resources Crime Prevention, Investigation, Prevention and Suppression Task Force will establish a practical geographical expert group composed of the relevant departments, units and provincial police commissions as necessary and necessary to the operation.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police stressed to the relevant specialized units, when returning, please report to the Commissioner or the head of the relevant unit, especially in any construction site involved in the crime.
