Neang Am rice farming community in Siem Reap uses drones, a modern technology for sowing rice
(Siem Reap): The Neang Am rice community in Siem Reap is becoming a modern agricultural community in Cambodia and is gaining traction as it implements modern drone technology for sowing rice at the beginning of the rainy season. The use of such modern technology makes the Srov Neang community save time, reduce costs and labor.
On May 23, 2024, the spokesman of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Khim Finang, congratulated the Srok Neang Am community for being able to afford to buy drones for farming, which is the most modern technology with the idea of saving money. The higher the community, the higher the cost of renting machinery or drones.
He said that the scale economy of large-scale joint farming makes the cost of renting a drone higher than the cost of buying a drone for regular use in the community, which is one of the main benefits of consolidating into a modern agricultural community. .
On May 6-10, 2024, Mr. Dith Tina, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, also visited Srov Neang Am community in Siem Reap province.
