(Phnom Penh): The representative of the French Development Agency (AFD) said that it will continue to invest in the water sector in Cambodia and expressed interest in co-financing green to small and medium enterprises in Cambodia, which will help both enterprises That is to embrace green technology, reduce emissions and move towards more sustainable business practices.
AFD's statement was made during a meeting between Minister of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation Hem Vandy and a delegation from the French Development Agency (AFD) led by Marie Helen Lerson to discuss special cooperation in the field of clean water on the 21st. May 2024.
For more than three decades, AFD has supported Cambodia in many areas, including infrastructure, education, and sustainable development.
Ms. Helen Lerson stated that the development of clean water infrastructure is one of the main goals of AFD in Cambodia to improve access to clean water and sanitation services by providing the necessary financing and technical assistance for the construction and rehabilitation of water supply systems, including the network. Distribution and water treatment plant.
She expressed interest in the green financing co-operation that AFD is implementing through Propaco to increase access to finance for small and medium enterprises as well as private water operators.
Mr. Hem Vandy thanked the French Development Agency for its continued good cooperation in the field of water, especially in Phnom Penh and Siem Reap, as well as its commitment to strengthen this cooperation.
The Minister said that due to the problem of climate change, the need to conserve water resources is important and cooperation in the field of clean water is essential for the development of Cambodia because it not only supports the livelihood of the people. Conserving the ecosystem and taking into account the environment as well.
He requested that AFD continue to strengthen the capacity of the Water Supply Authority to reach the nationwide coverage by expanding the water infrastructure in the capitals and provinces and preparing the water supply plan for each province.
Within the framework of green financing, the Minister requested AFD to examine the possibility of financing small and medium enterprises through cooperation with Cambodian entrepreneurs, emphasizing that financing is a catalyst for the growth of small and medium enterprises and continue to be enterprises. Large. At the same time, it helps enterprises to embrace green technology, reduce emissions and move towards more sustainable business practices.
He also requested that AFD cooperate with the Ministry on the development of national quality infrastructure to increase Cambodia's ability to export products to European and international markets.
