On the occasion of the opening of the first conference on "The future of Cambodia without genocide" this morning, May 22, 2024, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, a key figure in the peace process, said that the current stalemate Because other parties objected to the use of the words of the Cambodian state and did not even call the Khmer Rouge.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said: "This Paris Agreement is obstructed in connection with the issue that the opposition of the Khmer Rouge maintained its position from beginning to end to prosecute the Khmer Rouge, not just remember. "Thus, we propose to include in the Paris Agreement the prevention of the return of the genocidal regime."
The father of the victorious political founder explained that even in the Paris Peace Agreement, the other parties prevented the Khmer Rouge regime from being called a genocidal regime, and what was most unjust was that the country that recognized the Khmer Rouge regime continued. Provide political and military support to the Khmer Rouge and not only never admit their guilt to the Cambodian people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the issues related to the Khmer Rouge at the Paris International Conference, which began in 1989, his speech indicated that the most appropriate place for the Khmer Rouge is to try the International Criminal Court. Yes, in the SNC.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, at that time, the party of the State of Cambodia, represented by Samdech, demanded to prevent the return of the genocidal regime, but was stuck in this place by other parties not to mention the genocidal regime. After the stalemate, there was an escape to rely on Japan, and the Japanese side invited the prince for medical reasons, but the truth is a negotiation to find a point related to the language stalemate.
Negotiations later took place at a hotel from 7pm to 2:30 pm, with senior Japanese officials agreeing with Samdech Techo Hun Sen on the use of the term. Japan agreed with what Samdech Techo wanted, but if the agreement included the phrase "prevent the return of the genocidal regime", the Khmer Rouge or some other countries would not agree, so they decided to change it to "prevent the return. Acts from the new past.
