International Analysis: What is happening in the Gaza Strip is genocide?
What is genocide? The United Nations Convention on the Prevention and Torture of Genocide defines genocide as an act committed with the intent to destroy, in whole or in part, an ethnic group. Any race or religion. Acts that are classified as genocide include:
1. Murder of a member of a group Serious injury to the body and mind of members of the group. Intentionally causing a group to suffer a living situation designed for total or partial bodily harm. Establishment of measures aimed at preventing the birth of a baby Forced transfer of children from one group to another.
