Senior Minister Ieng Moly Holds a Meeting on Coordinating HIV / AIDS Response in Inspection
The purpose of this meeting is to present the achievements of the Cambodian HIV response in the past. Examine the dynamics of the joint system in response to HIV. Review and implement the rules of the National Policy on AIDS Eradication and Sustainability, AIDS Program, Inspection Sector.
Senior Minister Ieng Moly, President of the National AIDS Authority and Chair of the Meeting, welcomed the working group and the meeting, expressing their welcome and appreciation to the Ministry of Inspection for its efforts to participate in the implementation of the HIV response in the past. .
Mrs. V Srey Pov, Secretary of State and Chair of the AIDS Committee of the Ministry of Inspection, warmly welcomed the meeting and confirmed her participation in the HIV response through mainstreaming and dissemination through meetings and forums. Various. She announced the composition of the meeting from the Ministry of Inspection.
The Senior Minister gave the following comments and recommendations to the meeting: The Ministry of Inspection has been actively involved in the dissemination and dissemination of laws, including the AIDS Law, in order to eradicate AIDS, we must achieve 95 goals. 95-95.
The Ministry of Inspection shall prepare an HIV response plan and submit it to the Ministry of Economy and Finance by the deadline for requesting funding. Stigma and discrimination still exist in Cambodian society.
Despite measures to prevent HIV infection, new infections are still prevalent, especially among key young people. Exploring all the rules, regulations and methods of collection, especially private clinics to provide HIV response reports, we hope to achieve all three goals. The Ministry of Inspection shall attend monthly technical council meetings to review progress and technical work.
