The Ministry of Public Works held a meeting to discuss the process of submitting a joint bill for payment of water supply and wastewater service.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ros Vanna, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Technical Working Group, on May 20, 2024, chaired a meeting on the process of submitting a joint bill for payment of water supply. Clean and dirty water service.
The meeting was attended by Mr. Oum Sotha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation and Deputy Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Technical Working Group; General Department of Wastewater Treatment System, PPWSA in target provinces, including Siem Reap, Kampong Thom, Battambang, Kampot, Pursat and Kampong Cham.
The purpose of the meeting was to announce the validity of the work, the presentation of the background, progress and other technical work discussions in the procedure of submitting a joint bill for payment of water supply and wastewater service in the provinces. Targets include Siem Reap, Kampong Thom, Battambang, Kampot, Pursat and Kampong Cham.
As a result, the meeting decided to set out an action plan to carry out the work for the next two months by implementing the data collection and verification process between the water and wastewater connections in the six target provinces to start the procedure. Included as a joint bill for payment of water supply and wastewater service fee.
