A man stopped the car to buy clothes in Poipet City, suddenly a suspect drove in with both his son and an elderly mother in the car, the police chased after the suspect dumped the car
(Banteay Meanchey): A man, while stopping the car while the car was on fire to buy clothes, suddenly a suspect came and went in and drove away with both the son and the elderly mother of the car owner, causing alarm Surprised in Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province on the night of May 21, 2024.
Immediately after receiving this information, the Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Sithi Loh, Banteay Meanchey Provincial Police Commissioner, ordered the police force to cooperate with the relevant authorities to pursue and ambush the suspects. Eventually, the suspects dropped the two men and released The car was abandoned and fled.
While driving to buy clothes, a 13-year-old son, Sam Seila, and an 83-year-old mother, Ear Kimhor, waited in the car for about 10 minutes, when an unidentified person got into the car. Turn left along Standard Street, Nguon Bat.
When the suspect reached the heart pond, the suspect got the boy out of the car and continued on National Road 58 to the O'Neang intersection. Back.
Immediately after receiving the information from the people, the Major General, the Commissioner, led the Poipet City Police Inspectorate to conduct a patrol operation until the car was found at the association market and returned to its owner at 22: 230 minutes. The suspect escaped.
According to the General Commissioner, this case did not cause any injuries and the contents of the car with 2 mobile phones were stolen by the suspects. According to the son of the owner of the car after returning, the suspect also had a gun.
At this time, the relevant law enforcement forces have been working diligently to catch the perpetrators and punish them on the streets.
