Speech by Samdech Techo Hun Sen at the Closing Ceremony of the First Conference on "Cambodia's Future Without Genocide" on the morning of May 22, 2024. The conference was announced to open on May 20, 2024 under the chairmanship of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
Cambodia went through the genocidal regime of Pol Pot for 3 years, 8 months and 20 days after the Khmer Rouge overthrew the Lon Nol regime on April 17, 1975. The so-called killing field regime has killed nearly 3 million innocent people. On January 7, 1979, the remaining Cambodian citizens were liberated from death. The Khmer Rouge supreme leader was later tried by the Khmer Rouge tribunal, a hybrid tribunal of Cambodia and the United Nations.
However, in the past, some individuals, including the opposition, unfortunately propagated the day of liberation on January 7, the day to save the lives of the Cambodian people, as the day that Vietnam invaded Cambodia.
"If the United Nations, represented today, has a true verdict, it means that until the genocidal regime is born, we will prosecute it, and if it is judged, people will still say that there is no Khmer Rouge," he said. "No, there is no one to save them, they live on their own, so that is still a recurrence of history."
Samdech Techo stated that during the first visit of the Secretary-General of the United Nations (UN) Ban Ki-moon in October 2010, there were talks about the proceedings of the Khmer Rouge tribunal, with Ban Ki-moon demanding a trial on the case. In addition to the indictment of the Khmer Rouge leaders, many other high-ranking dignitaries were also indicted.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen described the UN claim as coercive, regardless of the consequences.
This is what Samdech Techo Hun Sen said on May 22, 2024, when he presided over the closing ceremony of the first conference on "The future of Cambodia without genocide".
Samdech Techo stated that justice is an important element of post-liberation national reconciliation. The courts of the former People's Republic of Kampuchea convicted the regime's leaders in 1979, but at that time the international community did not recognize the government that liberated the Cambodian people, nor did it recognize the justice that our courts had found.
"They condemned us for overthrowing the Khmer Rouge regime and even accused us of falsifying evidence related to the genocide," Hun Sen said.
"The Cambodian people are in great pain when the international community gives the Khmer Rouge a seat at the United Nations and imposes diplomatic and economic sanctions on the surviving Cambodian people," he said. From the Khmer Rouge regime for 12 years. The international community (some countries) even helped form the tripartite coalition government of Democratic Kampuchea in 1982 by supplying weapons and ammunition to the Khmer Rouge regime.
According to Samdech Techo, this is a repeated punishment for the victims and the blindfold of some countries for genocide. In the process of negotiating a political solution for Cambodia, Samdech made it clear that the most appropriate place for the Khmer Rouge was in the Court of Justice, not in the Supreme National Council of Cambodia (SNC).
This statement by Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on the occasion of Samdech presiding over the closing ceremony of the first conference on "The future of Cambodia without genocide" on the morning of May 22, 2024.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the lessons of history from the two mistakes that foreigners made on Cambodian soil are destructive: first, foreigners supported the coup to overthrow Prince Sihanouk until a genocidal war broke out, and second: support. Foreign goods to the Khmer Rouge seat at the United Nations and to impose diplomatic sanctions on the legitimate government, causing hardship to Cambodia. So please do not make a third mistake on Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen has said that if the international community adopts the same attitude of imposing sanctions on the Lon Nol regime as it does on Myanmar's current military regime, Cambodia may not fall into the hands of the Khmer Rouge who came to power and killed millions of innocent people. That person.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also raised questions and expressed regret that those countries had ever recorded in their internal notes that recognizing the Lon Nol regime was a mistake because it was not a democratic process? But unfortunately, Cambodia, a military coup, was recognized by the country that declared itself the father of democracy. For foreigners, they never admit that they have made serious mistakes in Cambodia.
"Second: Recognizing the Khmer Rouge sitting at the United Nations for 12 years and punishing those who tried to rise up against Pol Pot and starve here, so please do not make a third mistake on Cambodia because you Has already made two mistakes for Cambodia. This is an additional emphasis of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pain as some countries continued to support the representatives of the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime, which massacred millions of innocent Cambodians to remain at the United Nations for 12 years. Instead, they turned to imposing diplomatic sanctions and a 12-year economic blockade on the government that liberated the people from the abyss of death at the hands of the Khmer Rouge.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said this on May 22, 2024, on the occasion of his high presidency, closing the first conference on "The future of Cambodia without genocide".
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that the drafting of this law is not a violation of freedom of expression, but an end to the political game of some politicians.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "I would like to ask all lawmakers whether we can put a law in Cambodia or not for anyone who says that Cambodia does not have genocide is to be punished. Why do I have to dare to say that? A court verdict that Cambodia has a genocidal regime is conducting a genocidal trial. So, if the court verdict is issued, do we put a law to claim that Cambodia has a genocidal regime?
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the historical fact is that we really have a genocidal regime. The Khmer Rouge tribunal and the trial of the Khmer Rouge leaders is a fair trial for the Cambodian people, and Samdech and the Cambodian people have been waiting for up to 43 years.
Samdech Techo also stated that the verdict of the Khmer Rouge tribunal has ended the draw and has been recognized by the UN Security Council. The sum is zero because the United Nations condemns the atrocities of the Khmer Rouge but also condemns those who overthrew the Khmer Rouge.
The United Nations has defined genocide as the intentional genocide to destroy, in whole or in part, against a particular ethnic, racial, or religious group. Throughout history, many genocides have taken place in different parts of the world, from the war of expansion of the Mongol Empire to the Khmer Rouge regime that Cambodia once went through.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen presiding over the closing ceremony of the first conference on the future of Cambodia without genocide on the morning of May 22, 2024 at the Judicial Court Hall or the former Trial Chamber. Leading the Khmer Rouge.
