He then spent 45 years explaining how human beings, angels, and all beings understand how to alleviate suffering in life. All traces are born of jealousy, envy, jealousy, resentment, and ignorance of nature. If one tries to give up those misfortunes, one will attain true peace.
He has spent his whole life trying to save the world without discriminating against anyone. His advice has been an effective medicine to heal the suffering of the world from that time until today.
He passed away at the age of 80 on Tuesday, the 15th day of the full moon of the month of Pisak, in the year of the Snake, leaving his teachings, the Dharma, as a beacon for all beings.
Vesak is the day on which he was born, enlightened, and Nirvana. This Vesak festival is held to commemorate His Majesty the King, who sacrificed everything in his life to save all beings. Today, Vesak festival! Discover the festival, which is an important historical day of all Buddhists all over the world.
Today is also the day that the United Nations has designated Vesak as an International Day since December 15, 1999, which is a universal recognition of the contribution of Buddhism to the world for more than two thousand six hundred years. This is and is continuing to contribute to uplifting the spirit of humanity. United Nations offices everywhere are closed on this sacred day.
We always think that the Vaisakhi worship is only once a year and the worship is only once a year. In fact, the Buddha enlightened that the best sacrifice, the supreme sacrifice, is to follow the Dharma and sacrifice without spending wealth.
Vesak is celebrated every day: the commemoration of the Buddha's birthday, the anniversary of enlightenment and the anniversary of the Buddha's Nirvana should also be celebrated every day. I would like to take the Buddha as a place of remembrance, a word that we always recite, we have to take as a basis every day, even though we have to follow the monks only three times.
We can take the meaning of Vesak as a guide for our daily life as follows:
1. Birthday: Born to be determined to do something, create something new in life until it is achieved by studying, training, educating yourself through the seven ancestral steps, the middle path, the four noble truths that the Buddha advanced before us and Already decided.
2. Enlightenment Day: When you have achieved what you set out to do, you should make it happen for the benefit of yourself and humanity, and share the accomplishments and ways that lead to that goal to all mankind.
3. Nirvana: Death is the nature of all human beings. As a person before death, there should be some legacy that the next generation can use to build themselves, society and the environment to be sustainable in the long run.
On this auspicious day, as Buddhists, we must strive to learn Buddhism to understand and apply Buddhism on a daily basis in order to preserve Buddhism as a state religion and spread the teachings of the Buddha on peace. Wisdom and compassion for the Khmer people and the next generation of human beings in a comprehensive way.
