This Morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen Presides Over the Closing Ceremony of the First Conference on the Future of Cambodia Without Genocide
The first conference on "The future of Cambodia without genocide" was announced on May 20, 2024 under the chairmanship of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The conference is an important forum to highlight the role of crime education and mental and physical health care in preventing and responding to genocide. Education about violent crime is crucial to ensuring that individuals and society are aware of their past.
Knowledge, along with an understanding of the ongoing impact of these crimes, is an important first step in cultivating the necessary mindfulness and attention to prevent future potentially dangerous situations. Successful education on atrocities requires the strong commitment of the government and civil society.
The conference aims to build a multi-ethnic community by bringing together experts on human rights and genocide prevention in post-conflict countries who can share ideas and best practices to work together to build lasting peace in the country. Cambodia and the world.
In response to the crime prevention and response policy, the conference aims to create campaigns to ensure that governments around the world integrate crime education into their national high school curriculum.
Participants in the conference discussed ways to work together to achieve the commitment of military forces around the world to integrate brutal crime education as a core component of military professional education to military officers and ranks. Leading senior military.
Most importantly, the conference seeks to develop a strategy to integrate criminal education into international development policy by urging donors to impose conditions on recipients to develop a brutal crime education program. One that is reliable in its education system.
The three-day conference was held with a variety of programs, including discussions on key topics such as genocide, justice, youth and health education. There will also be a visit to learn about health, human rights and transitional justice. The Ministry of Water Resources announces the weather situation in Cambodia for May 22, 2024.
