He said that at present, the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port has been working with the Cambodian Rice Federation from any destination market.
Oknha Chan Sokheang, President of the Cambodian Rice Federation, told Fresh News on May 21, 2024 that the Rice Federation is looking at markets such as the Middle East, China and Southeast Asia to use this means of transportation.
He said that this means of transport is an alternative to container shipping because in the past, the export of rice by container sometimes encountered obstacles due to the lack of container shells, especially delivery to nearby markets such as in the country. Indonesia, Philippines, Malaysia and so on. Therefore, shipping to these markets is a good and cost-effective option.
He said that when Cambodia began to export large quantities of goods to a number of markets, especially the Southeast Asian market, the Middle East, the use of this means of transportation is a good choice because the major markets always use the basic means of transportation.
Please be informed that more than 95% of Cambodian rice exported uses Sihanoukville Port. The port is examining the possibility of equipping additional cranes and warehousing facilities to allow pre-ship rice collection, which could enable Cambodia to export 6,000 tonnes to 20,000 tonnes of rice per ship in the near future. .
