Understand the Justice Court or the Khmer Rouge Tribunal
(Phnom Penh): The Judicial Court is a historic site that was once one of the few courts in the world serving justice and international criminal law. Moreover, the Judicial Court is considered to be one of the few courts that support the successful prosecution of genocidal crimes.
The Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia (ECCC) was established to support criminal proceedings committed by senior leaders of the Democratic Kampuchea regime and individuals most responsible for serious violations of national and international law during the regime. Democratic Kampuchea (April 17, 1975 to January 6, 1979).
The Judiciary Hall is an important historical site for remembering the stories and work involved in the Khmer Rouge tribunal case, as well as the difficult process of seeking justice that continues to this day. In 2022, after 16 years of operation, the Extraordinary Chambers in the Courts of Cambodia closed its historic mission and returned the hall to the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
After the handing over of the Judicial Court to the Army Command, Samdech Moha Bovathibodi Hun Manet, former Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, recommended that the Justice Hall be preserved for the history of the next generation of Cambodians. To understand the trial process of former senior leaders of the Khmer Rouge.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun sets strict guidelines for Svay Rieng province to eradicate drug use in entertainment locations
(Svay Rieng): Dr. Neth Savoeun, Deputy Prime Minister, Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs and Chairman of the 9th Anti-Illegal Drug Campaign Command, has set out a strict policy for Svay Rieng Province to completely eliminate piracy. Illegal drugs of all kinds at entertainment locations throughout the province.
This morning, May 21, 2024, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun introduced the principles of the 9th Anti-Drug Campaign Plan of the Provincial Drug Control Committee. Svay Rieng. This meeting was held to ensure the effectiveness of the successful implementation of the campaign.
Dr. Neth Savoeun set out three main principles for the Svay Rieng Provincial Drug Control Committee, including: educational measures, administrative measures and legal measures. At this point, he stressed the need to end all phenomena that hinder the implementation of this elimination operation and, if necessary, immediately report to the national level to intervene.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the National Authority for Combating Drugs urged the Provincial Administrative Unity Command to hold a meeting with the owners of various entertainment venues to guide and request their participation in supporting the eradication campaign. However, he stressed that in case of non-cooperation, immediate legal action must be taken.
Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun also reminded the Provincial Administrative Unity Command and the authorities at all levels of Svay Rieng Province to work together to strictly implement the direction of Samdech Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia "Clean the Lake". All officers must be clean and not involved in drugs.
In addition, Mr. Sandibandit, Deputy Prime Minister, urged to pay attention to increase and strengthen the effectiveness of education to the people by making it up to date and targeted easily. While the installation of the mobile app (App) "NoDrug" must be done at the same time, because this app contains both educational messages and a way for people to report to the relevant authorities in drug cases.
Separately, for those who fall into the trap of drugs, Deputy Prime Minister Neth Savoeun advised to encourage and promote the transfer to treatment facilities and rehabilitation centers for the opportunity to reintegrate into society.
