PM Hun Manet Receives Deputy Director General of the French Development Agency
It should be noted that the French Development Agency (AFD) opened its office in Phnom Penh in September 1993 to intervene in Cambodia. AFD was initially focused on financing agriculture, urban development and health.
Since July 2009, AFD's means of intervention in Cambodia have evolved significantly. To support Cambodia's economic growth, AFD has partnered with the Cambodian authorities to support the manufacturing sector through unsecured lending, meaning loans provided directly to enterprises or private or public banks. Guaranteed by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Moreover, since July 2012, Cambodia has been able to obtain concessional loans from AFD after receiving a better rating from the International Monetary Fund for its ability to repay its debt.
Currently, the four priority areas of AFD interventions are: agriculture and agro-industry, infrastructure, production support, vocational training: (in textiles and tourism and agriculture, if possible).
