The Ministry of Interior summoned Brigadier General Keo Saravuth to clarify immediately on the case of collecting 1 million Riel per commune from 10 communes in Samaki Monichey district
(Phnom Penh): After spreading the news on social media about the case of a general in the General Department of Internal Audit of the Ministry of Interior related to taking 1 million Riels per commune from 10 communes in Samaki Monchey district, Kampong Speu province, Mr. Dr. Sar Sokha, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, has submitted a policy to the Ministry of Interior's General Inspectorate to investigate the case immediately.
Receiving this principle, on the morning of May 21, 2024, the Inspectorate of the Ministry of Interior sent a working group to invite Brigadier General Keo Saravuth, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Internal Audit of the Ministry of Interior to immediately comment at the Inspectorate. This was confirmed by Mr. Touch Sok, Deputy Spokesman of the Ministry of Interior.
Mr. Touch Sokak further stated that as a result, after clarification, Brigadier General Keo Saravuth admitted that he had actually led a 7-member audit team in Kampong Speu Province from April 24, 2024 by using his own vehicle. 2 units and only 4 districts have been audited.
As a follow-up procedure, the Ministry of Interior will review this case further based on the facts and based on the discipline of the Cambodian National Police Force.
Mr. Touch Sokak further asserted that the Ministry of Interior would like to reassure the public that for the effectiveness of the reform work in line with the Royal Government's Pentagon strategy and the "Clean House" vision of Prime Minister Hun Manet, the Prime Minister of Cambodia. Advertising and public opinion are very important.
In this regard, the Ministry of Interior encourages and takes into consideration all the information related to the field under its jurisdiction, especially information on cases of irregularities in the performance of duties of civil servants, national police officers and prison officials at all levels. As well as requests, suggestions and opinions of people from all walks of life.
Mr. Touch Sokak added that the Ministry of Interior also needs to work together to fight all false information, unprofessional advertising and negative intentions.
