However, Dr. Yong Pov and Ambassador Chin Po agree that both countries (Cambodia and China) should focus on their national interests and continue to develop and strengthen Cambodian relations. - China to grow steadily rather than focus on those unreasonable criticisms.
Dr. continued that the relationship between Cambodia and China, which has lasted for more than 2,000 years, is a relationship that has the highest historical character and closeness, as evidenced by the existing temples of Angkor Wat and Bayon in Cambodia. In addition, 2024 is a year of diamond cooperation and a year of people-to-people contacts, a period in which the two countries need to strengthen ties better than ever.
However, according to Dr. Yong Pov, this bilateral relationship has also been criticized by the United States, which rivals China and Vietnam, which are members of the ASEAN region and are in territorial disputes with China. For Dr. Cambodia-China need to further strengthen the relationship, in which the two countries must promote the development of Cambodia to be stronger as a strong foreign relations in Southeast Asia.
Ambassador Chin Po agreed with Dr. Yong Pov's statement, emphasizing that "the two countries have their own sovereignty and can cooperate without having to worry about other countries outside." Ambassador Chin Po said that China-Cambodia relations are very important and the discussions in the brain banking forum between the two countries will further promote the relationship between the two countries.
Overall, Dr. Yong Pov and Ambassador Chin Po expressed the common view that Cambodia and China need to further strengthen bilateral relations in all fields and continue their national development path in accordance with the needs and ideals. In the national interest, rather than worrying about accusations in the sense of obstruction from foreigners.
In addition, Dr. Yong Pov and Ambassador Chin Po also expressed the same belief that strengthening the joint voice between Cambodia and China to strengthen the strength of the two countries in the international arena is key. The Ministry of Environment is looking for partners to order drones to hand over to the Department of Environment to modernize natural resource protection areas more effectively.
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Eang Sophalleth, Minister of the Ministry of Environment, said that the Ministry of Environment is looking for partners and funds to order drones to be handed over to the Department of Environment to modernize the protection of natural resources in its jurisdiction more effectively. Next month, the ministry will receive satellite maps for distribution to the Provincial Unity Command in order to facilitate the prevention of illegal encroachment on forest land.
This statement was made by Dr. Eang Sophalleth on the morning of May 20, 2024, when he presided over a press conference before the exhibition and distribution of seedlings under the theme "Green Sprouts". From July 10-16.
Dr. Eang Sophalleth said that the Ministry of Environment is working with partner organizations to ensure that satellite imagery reflects natural resource protection areas and cleared sites.
Dr. expressed hope that when the Ministry of Environment receives the map from the satellite, the Ministry will send it to the Capital, Provincial Administrative Command, National Armed Forces, Anti-Corruption Unit and the Department of Environment, which has a natural resource protection area for viewing. Clearly see which cabinets are being encroached upon by crooks.
With the receipt of additional maps related to natural resource protection areas, the Minister of Environment confirmed that no later than next month, the Ministry will receive this map from partner organizations next month for distribution to all stakeholders.
"Through satellite data and the provision of drones, local officials can study and obtain information on the location of illegal encroachment on forest land and enable authorities to prevent crime in a timely manner." This is an additional statement of Dr. Eang Sophalleth.
He added that the Ministry of Environment is developing a digital app to improve the management of Cambodia's 73 protected areas, covering about 7 million hectares, or 40 percent of the country's land area.
It should be noted that the Ministry of Environment recently handed over 132 A0 and A3 size protected area maps to 21 provincial administrations and 111 district administrations in response to the first phase of the Pentagon strategy of the Royal Government. 7 and in accordance with the green and sustainable nature of the environmental strategy in the context of environmental correctness.
ASEAN Secretary-General kicks off visit to Japan, visits Hiroshima Peace Memorial Museum and meets Hiroshima city leaders
The ASEAN Secretary-General visited the Hiroshima Peace Memorial Museum, the site of the World War II nuclear bombing of Hiroshima.
After visiting the museum, the ASEAN Secretary-General signed the museum's Golden Book, gave interviews to the local media and laid a wreath in memory of those killed in the Paramano bombing at the park. Memories of Hiroshima peace as well.
It is important to note that Hiroshima was the first city in the world to be hit by a nuclear bomb and rebuilt from the ashes. As a supporter of peace, ASEAN is committed to working closely with the world to ensure a nuclear-weapon-free zone and prevent the proliferation of nuclear weapons in the region and the world.
On that occasion, the two sides exchanged views on ASEAN-Japan relations, including possible reciprocal exchanges and fraternal cooperation between Hiroshima and other ASEAN cities.
Dr. Kao Kim Hourn Encouraged Hiroshima to Contribute to Strengthening ASEAN-Japan Cooperation, Supporting ASEAN Efforts on the Elimination and Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons by Continuing to Promote the Southeast Asia Nuclear-Weapon-Free Treaty (SEANWFZ Treaty).
