(Siem Reap): For 25 years (1999-2024), Angkor Hospital for Children of Siem Reap has made significant contributions to the examination, treatment and care of millions of Cambodian children to achieve good health. Angkor Hospital for Children recently published its six-month results report from October 2023 to March 2024.
In addition to treating and caring for patients, Angkor Hospital for Children is also a training center. Angkor Hospital for Children provided health education to people in target areas in Siem Reap and Preah Vihear with more than 270,000 participants. With an estimated 9,000 other participants through training of health officials, medical students and interns, as well as staff of Angkor children.
Dr. Nguon Chanpheaktra, Director of Angkor Hospital for Children, said, “I am very grateful for the support of all of you for 25 years. "These results are the result of the support and encouragement of local and international philanthropists, volunteers, board of staff, Angkor Hospital for Children and the Royal Government of Cambodia, which is full of generosity, loyalty and commitment."
It should also be noted that every year, Angkor Hospital for Children needs about 6 million US dollars to operate Angkor Hospital for Children through three main activities: medical examination and treatment in the hospital, medical education and preventive education programs. Community health.
The hospital calls on philanthropists, companies and institutions at all levels to continue to provide as much assistance as possible to save the lives of children in need of treatment, health care, medical training and to provide community health prevention education.
