(Phnom Penh): Cambodian youths must hurry to receive vocational training from 1.5 million poor and vulnerable families in order to gain real skills and accelerate family life while vocational training schools TVET across the country is always ready to train.
This was stated by Mr. Hing Sideth, Director General of the General Department of Technical and Vocational Education and Training on the occasion of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training organized a visit to journalists by the Polytechnic Institute of Cambodia (NPIC) in late May 2024. This.
On that occasion, Director General Hing Sideth said, "TVET's policy is to provide real skills to poor and vulnerable families so that a citizen has at least one skill in life, when there is a clear skill is money "Regular income helps support themselves and their families, as well as society."
He said that when enrolling, students also received advice on 38 subjects, while recently added 7 more subjects, a total of 45 subjects covering 10 fields. All are majors with high demand in the job market.
For the education and training program for young people from poor and vulnerable 1.5 million families, there is also a lot of flexibility for young people who have a job, in which the study is divided into 3 shifts: the first shift of study From Monday-Friday during the day for 4 months, the second shift is the night shift from 5:30 to 8:30 for 8 months and the third shift is Saturday-Sunday for 10 months Months.
Mr. Hing Sideth, General Director, continued that the training is in line with the national qualification framework, in line with the current and future labor market. He said that currently TVET skills training for students is not enough to meet the needs of the labor market 100 percent, that is, there are still more needs, which is an opportunity for young people to enroll in TVET skills.
Mr. Hing Sideth stated that the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has also signed agreements with the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and at least 18 employers' associations to accept trainees for internship and recruitment of trainees to work in the enterprise. Body with a decent salary.
He added that students who have graduated and will go to work with a regular income if they want to continue their studies while improving their skills, they can also come to study. Learning TVET skills such as bridges, students continue their studies to higher education as well.
It should be informed that out of the approximately 20,000 students who have studied with the education and training program for young people from poor and vulnerable families, the first step has been training gradually, while they also receive some support. From the owner of the enterprise as well. For the second phase, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training will be ready to accept at least 30,000 more registered students.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanks the Czech Republic for canceling its debt and turning the remaining debt into development aid
According to Samdech Techo, the Czech Republic will continue to provide assistance in the areas of health, education and human resource development, especially in the field of education, providing scholarships to Cambodian students to study in the Czech Republic.
Samdech Techo welcomed and expressed his pleasure to meet the Ambassador of the Czech Republic to Cambodia in his new role as President of the Senate now. Samdech Techo hopes that the Ambassador will continue to work to strengthen the relationship between the two countries.
In response, the Ambassador expressed his pleasure to meet with Samdech at this time and also congratulated Samdech Techo on his new role as President of the Senate of the Kingdom of Cambodia, a higher position. He also said that during 2019, during Samdech Techo PM's visit to the Czech Republic, the two sides pledged to continue cooperation in development assistance in the fields of education and health.
Samdech Techo expressed his gratitude for the wishes and Samdech Techo confirmed to him that in his role as President of the Senate, he has set the promotion of parliamentary diplomacy as one of the priorities of the Senate in this new pity, with an important role in promoting international relations. Cambodia In this spirit, the Senate is ready to work with the Czech Ambassador to further deepen bilateral cooperation between the two countries.
Regarding bilateral relations between Cambodia and the Czech Republic, Samdech Techo expressed his satisfaction that since 1979, despite the fact that Czechoslovakia has been divided and the political situation in Cambodia has changed, the relations between the two countries continue and Samdech Techo The prince is said to have had close relations with the leaders of the Czech Republic.
Regarding the promotion of parliamentary diplomacy, the Ambassador informed the Prince that he would make efforts to facilitate the Czech Republic Parliamentary delegation to visit Cambodia later this year, as the Czech Republic Parliamentary delegation intends to Come and visit Cambodia as well.
Samdech Techo also encouraged efforts to increase trade volume between the two countries, especially to balance the trade balance by increasing the export of goods from Cambodia to the Czech Republic, as well as from the Czech Republic to Cambodia more. At the same time, the prince also recommended that any agreement be considered, which could encourage investors to trust each other, as well as encourage investment between the two countries.
Finally, Samdech Te Chea also wished the Ambassador of the Czech Republic success in his mission in Cambodia and encouraged the cooperation between the two countries to continue to grow stronger and better.
