(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia on May 20, 2024 released the report on financial stability in 2023, in which Dr. Chea Serey, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia said that the Cambodian economy is projected to An increase of 6% with an inflation rate of around 2% in 2024.
Dr. Chea Serey made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the workshop on "Financial Stability Report 2023" organized by the National Bank of Cambodia on May 20, 2024.
Dr. Chea Serey said that this is the sixth annual report released by the National Bank of Cambodia to raise awareness of the economic and financial situation and provide a perspective on financial stability.
"Cambodia's economy is projected to grow by 6% by 2024 with an inflation rate of around 2%. Growth is mainly supported by exports of garments and non-garments. "Tourism and related sectors and strong growth in the transport and telecommunications sector, while the agricultural sector may continue to grow slowly."
In addition, the implementation of the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP) and Bilateral Free Trade Agreements (FTAs) is expected to contribute to attracting more investment and exports to the region, he added. Promote productivity and economic diversification.
"However, the Cambodian economy faces a number of risks, such as tensions and geopolitical divisions, prolonged tightening of the international financial situation, slower-than-expected growth of the Chinese economy, and climate change," said Dr. Chea Serey. And increased cyber risk. "All of these risks could lead to a slowdown in global economic and trade activity, which could also affect exports, investment and capital flows to Cambodia."
