Samdech President Hun Manet: We must continue to talk about genocide from generation to generation, even if these stories cause pain (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech President Hun Manet said that we must acknowledge That genocide education is a mechanism to prevent genocide, and he said that we must continue to talk about genocide from generation to generation, even if it hurts.
"We must continue to tell these stories from generation to generation, even if they are painful," said Hun Sen. "This is the most effective way because only those who have been through it can best describe their experience."
He said that the mistakes of the past have told us to unite the Khmer nation strongly and urge us to build a better society with an environment for all. It is the duty of the government to promote good governance and social justice to ensure the environment in the management system as well as national development.
Hun Manet also said that genocide education does not have to be limited to history lessons. We can also integrate all subjects from Khmer morality and literature to leadership studies and other soft skills development.
According to the President, we can also find creative ways to tell these difficult stories to people of different ages and generations, including through art, digital content or animation.
