The conference on "Cambodia's Future Without Genocide" will be held for three days from May 20 to 22. The President of the Senate of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, will preside over the closing ceremony of the conference on May 22.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Mani President Hun Manet's opportunity to chair the opening conference on the future of Cambodia without genocide:
* President Hun Manet stated that today's meeting is an expression of recognition of the role of the Khmer Rouge Tribunal.
* President Hun Manet stated that the organization of the conference on the day of Remembrance Day was not a coincidence.
Samdech Hun Sen eth reminded that the memory of the genocide is a reminder to the Cambodian nation to prevent this act from coming back.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that January 7, 1979 was the second birthday of the Cambodian people from the genocidal regime.
* Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet stated that the agreement to compile documents related to the genocidal regime is an important task for the education of the next generation of Cambodian children.
* President Hun Manet stated that seeking internationally recognized justice is an effective way to establish a common history of genocide for all, regardless of political affiliation.
* President Hun Manet stated that on the basis of justice, society as a whole must continue to be reminded of the roots of past tragedies in order to allow the most difficult experiences of the past to contribute to a better defense of Cambodia in the future.
* President Hun Manet stated that society must constantly remind lessons to ensure that Cambodia does not walk the same path. In addition, the social situation must be adjusted or adapted, whenever necessary, to prevent extremist ideology from emerging and taking root in Cambodian society.
* President Hun Manet stated that no component of society can be allowed to re-emerge from the extremist political culture by inciting class struggle, hatred against the authorities, regime change contrary to democratic principles, and Racial discrimination.
* Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated that the mistakes of the past have told us to unite the Khmer nation firmly and encourage us to build a better society with an environment for all. It is the duty of the government to promote good governance and social justice to ensure the environment in the management system as well as national development.
* President Hun Manet stated that we must recognize that genocide education is a mechanism to prevent genocide.
* President Hun Manet stated that we must continue to tell these stories from one generation to the next, even if these stories are painful. This is the most effective way because only those who have been through it can best describe their experience.
* President Hun Manet stated that genocide education is not limited to history lessons. We can also integrate all subjects from Khmer morality and literature to leadership studies and other soft skills development.
* Samdech Hun Manet added that we can also find creative ways to tell these difficult stories to people of different ages and generations, including through art, digital content or animation.
Samdech Hun Sen stated that today's conference is a good example of good cooperation and solidarity between various stakeholders.
* President Hun Manet stated that in order to prevent the genocidal regime, peace must be maintained.
* President Hun Manet stated that when war breaks out, there is no human rights, no democracy.
* Samdech Hun Manet stated that all future leaders of Cambodia must refrain from participating in political plans that promote undemocratic regime change and must adhere to a sense of responsibility in safeguarding peace.
* President Hun Manet stated that Cambodia continues to defend itself against malicious fabrications aimed at Cambodia's reputation window and against any attempt to plunge Cambodia into the trap of geopolitical competition and turn Cambodia into To a new Cold War battle.
