(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ky Tech, Chairman of the Royal Government Lawyers Group, shows three telephone numbers for victims involved in the company of Ms. Leng Channa to contact and to receive protection of legal rights and interests.
On May 13, 2024, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, authorized Mr. Ky Tech to lead the Royal Government's lawyer to protect the rights and interests of the victims of Ms. Leng Channa's company.
After receiving this right, Mr. Ky Tech and members of the Royal Government Law Team followed the high order of the Prime Minister with a high sense of responsibility in order to protect the rights and interests of the victims in accordance with the procedure. And the law in force in all relevant authorities and tribunals at all levels.
According to Mr. Kitech, after announcing the phone number within 3 days, received about 1,500 representatives of the victims.
On May 16, 2024, 31 people contacted the working group and claimed to be representatives of about 1,400 affected people.
On May 17, 19 people contacted the working group and claimed that about 100 representatives of the victims.
On May 18, five people contacted the team who claimed to be victims in the same case.
In a meeting with Cambodians in South Korea, President Hun Manet confirmed that he was not silent on the fraud case and was taking legal action and finding a solution for the victims. The Royal Government continues to search for people involved in this scam to deal with the law as well.
It should be noted that in this case of hundreds of millions of dollars fraud, the authorities have arrested Ms. Leng Channa and a total of eight people as of May 19, 2024.
