Mr. Neth Pheaktra donated 27 million Riels to the staff to restore Boeung Kon Sat in Chhlong district to irrigate nearly 700 hectares of people's agricultural land
(Kratie): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Minister of Information and Chairman of Kratie Provincial Government Working Group, handed over 27 million Riels from the participation of Kratie Provincial Leaders and Working Group to the Department of Public Works and Transport. Transport of Kratie province to restore the baby lake in Prek Saman commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province on May 18, 2024 at Chhlong district hall.
The lake covers an area of 51 hectares and can hold millions of cubic meters of water to irrigate 694 hectares of people's agricultural land. The people who benefit from this lake are 512 families with 5,560 people.
Mr. CHAN Saphan said that the initiative in rehabilitating the lake, seeing the difficulties of the people in Prek Saman commune, Chhlong district, Kratie province, especially the farmers who enjoy growing crops around Boeung Koun. Animals that have experienced a shortage of water sources for irrigating rice in recent years.
He confirmed that the work to restore the lake is using machinery, costing 40,000 liters of fuel and equivalent to more than 40,000 dollars. In addition, he also contributed to the restoration of this lake in the amount of 10,000 dollars, and also you, as a national and provincial government working group, also contributed to help restore the lake to achieve the project. Plan laid out.
The Secretary of State also stated that the lake will be rehabilitated on an area of 51 hectares on 694 hectares of arable land, equivalent to 512 families, which is a large reservoir for farmers in the whole Prek Saman commune. In pumping water for irrigating your fields to get high yields and be able to farm two to three times a year, depending on the ability of the farmers.
