Preah Serey Kosal Som Sokha was elected as the Chairman of the Board of Directors of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia for the 7th mandate, succeeding Samdech Preah Moha Arey Vong Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat
(Phnom Penh): In the afternoon of May 18, 2024, the General Assembly of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia held a meeting to elect 33 new members of the Board of Directors to continue to lead the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia for the seventh mandate. Sokha Preah Chao Athikar Wat Phnea Simpaly was elected Chairman of the Board of Directors of the 7th mandate, succeeding His Majesty the King Dr. Yorn Seng Yeat.
The State Buddhist Association of Cambodia is an organization that has played an important role in humanitarian work in the Cambodian Buddhist society. This association has been an important part of the Board of Priests of the Kingdom of Cambodia since the beginning, especially the King and Queen, who are highly revered, and His Majesty the King is honored to be the Honorary President of the Association. This is forever.
Leaders of the Senate, the National Assembly, the Royal Government, government officials and Buddhists in many countries have also joined, supported, promoted and volunteered for membership. This proves that the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia is one of the potential humanitarian associations in the Cambodian Buddhist society.
