Please note that Cambodia and South Korea were officially established diplomatic relations on October 30, 1997. This diplomatic bond was re-established under the strong efforts of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, or Samdech Techo as a midwife, to establish relations between Cambodia and South Korea. After the formal establishment, relations and cooperation between the two countries have been strengthened, expanded and enhanced to become stronger and better.
Through better relations, Cambodia and South Korea have also expanded trade and investment together in significant growth. Trade between the two countries in 2023 will have a total budget of about 751 million US dollars. In the first three months of 2024, it will reach nearly 200 million US dollars.
Cambodia's main exports to Korea in 2023: machinery and electrical equipment, footwear, clothing and accessories, aluminum, machinery and mechanical equipment, leather goods, toys, sports equipment, pharmaceutical products, plastics, paper and cardboard, rubber, fruits and Edible nuts and so on.
Cambodia's main imports from Korea in 2023 include vehicles, machinery, electrical appliances, beverages, wine and vinegar, raw leather (besides leather), leather, plastics, pharmaceuticals, other textiles, rubber, machinery and mechanical equipment.
