Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandith Return to Cambodia After a Successful Visit to South Korea
(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, and His Excellency Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet returned to Cambodia at almost 9 pm on May 18, 2024, after concluding their official visit. In the territory of the Republic of Korea or South Korea for 4 days.
Departing from Seoul, the President and Lok Chumteav Bandit and the delegation were accompanied by the Korean Ambassador to Cambodia, the Cambodian Ambassador to Korea, senior officials of the Korean Ministry of Foreign Affairs and other Cambodian officials in Korea. .
Please be reminded that at the invitation of Mr. Yoon Seok-yol, President of the Republic of Korea, Prime Minister Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Bandith led the delegation to pay their first official visit as the Prime Minister of South Korea on the morning of the 15th. May 2024.
The current visit of Samdech Manet to South Korea focuses on enhancing cooperation, trade and investment between Cambodia and South Korea.
Regarding political affairs, President Hun Manet met with South Korean President Yoon Seok-yol, South Korean Prime Minister Han Dok-soo, and South Korean National Assembly President Kim Jong-un.
Through these meetings, Samdech Hun Sen and the top leaders of South Korea expressed their satisfaction with the excellent diplomatic relations and cooperation between Cambodia and South Korea for nearly 30 years, both politically, economically and socially. And culture.
During the summit between Hun Manet and Yun Sokyol, the two leaders discussed bilateral cooperation, covering key areas including politics, economy and trade, infrastructure development, defense and security, and more.
During his current visit to South Korea, President Hun Manet demonstrated his high commitment to enhancing relations and cooperation between Cambodia and South Korea through the decision to enhance relations. "Strategic Partnership", a high-level relationship.
In addition to agreeing to upgrade relations to "strategic partners", the two countries have signed six more important documents to strengthen trade and investment cooperation and support development in Cambodia.
Foreign investment is an important part of building the national economy to grow, create jobs, generate income and improve the lives of Cambodians. For this reason, every time he visits abroad, whether on an official visit or within the framework of meetings, Samdech Hun Sen never misses a meeting with foreign investors.
During his first visit to South Korea as the Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet made great efforts to attract Korean investment to Cambodia.
On Friday, May 17, 2024, from early morning to late evening, Samdech Hun Manet received a series of meetings with Korean investors with a total of up to nine. Meetings took place from company to company, with no breaks, not even lunch.
In a meeting with the leaders of companies that some companies are doing business in Cambodia and some companies are not doing business in Cambodia yet, Samdech Hun Sen tried to persuade them to expand more investment capital for companies doing business in Cambodia, while companies are not yet doing business. Ask for a visit to learn about investment opportunities.
Hun Manet strives to present favorable conditions for the benefits of investment in Cambodia, such as a peaceful country, stable young labor force, wide market space, combined with the policy of providing high protection to investors from the Royal Government.
Through his persuasive efforts and explanations, the company's management has expressed its satisfaction with the investment in Cambodia. The companies that are investing are expressing their intention to expand their investment, while the companies that have not yet invested are coming to Cambodia to find out and find opportunities for their investment.
In addition, Samdech President Hun Manet also presided over the opening of the Cambodia-Republic of Korea Business Forum. The Cambodia-Republic of Korea Business Forum, organized by the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce and the Chamber of Commerce and Industry of the Republic of Korea, was attended by more than 300 Cambodian and Korean investors representing 198 companies.
Before returning to Cambodia, Samdech Hun Sen also met with the Cambodian community living, studying and working in South Korea.
During the meeting, Samdech Hun Sen presented the results of the visit, presenting the Royal Government's policies and taking into account the lives of Cambodians in South Korea.
Samdech President Hun Manet also confirmed the legal action against Leng Channa and his cronies who created a scheme to deceive the people, including those living in Korea.
Samdech Hun Sen also thanked the Cambodian people in Korea for supporting the Funan Techo Canal Project, which is in the common interest of Cambodia. Samdech Thipadei confirmed that the project will start opening soon.
The Prime Minister also called on the people to trust that he will strive to maintain peace, promote national development and reduce the poverty of the people as much as possible.
