Mr. Ley Sopheap calls on all citizens to be aware of eye health and eye examination regularly
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Ley Sopheap, President of the Cambodian Federation of Medical, Pharmacological and Dental Associations and President of the Cambodian Pharmacists Association, said that people at all levels must know how to take care of their eyes because eyes are life and must understand the factors that cause To have eye problems and disease, especially should check the eyes regularly to avoid problems before seeking treatment.
The above statement of the President of the Association of the Federation of Medical, Pharmaceutical and Dentistry of Cambodia was made during the ceremony of recognizing the Chairman and Vice Chairman of the Eye Care Committee on May 18, 2024 at the association's headquarters in Chroy Changvar district.
He said the eye care committee aims to support people in the community who sell ophthalmology, ophthalmology and eye hospitals. In addition, the Eye Care Commission is established with the support of all relevant units and is responsible for separating the most vulnerable people from low to severe eye problems to encourage and guide care or treatment according to their specialties. .
On this occasion, Dr. Ley Sopheap instructed the Chairman of the Eye Care Commission to collect input from all ophthalmologists and eye hospitals in Cambodia, including vendors and cut glasses to make sure all parties involved. Collaborate to carry out work to help the health of the people and businesses do this so that all stakeholders benefit, that is, citizens can understand the well-being.
The lens is an important part of the human body. Each of us has at least one eye problem in our life. Some minor problems can be easily treated, while others require specialized medical attention. That is why all of us should pay attention to maintaining eye health.
In the above ceremony, Dr. Ley Sopheap said, "Eyes are like life, losing eyes is almost a loss of life, so what to do to take good care of the eyes."
Taking this opportunity, Dr. Ley Sopheap advised the people "If possible, should have regular eye examinations to avoid problems to find treatment and treatment needs a doctor."
The Eye Care Commission aims to contribute to the Royal Government as well as to help educate people about eye health issues, especially in the community.
At the same time, Dr. Tith Sam Oeun, Member Representative of the Eye Care Committee, is committed to educating and disseminating eye care knowledge to the community and strengthening the professional capacity of all members, as well as expanding the eye care team throughout Cambodia. Also.
Mr. Hor Mao, a security guard in Meanchey district, who facilitated traffic for the people in Chak Angre Krom, died of a heart attack
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Hor Mao, the administrative security guard of Meanchey district, who facilitated traffic for the people in Chak Angre Krom, passed away at 3:00 pm on May 18, 2024 at the age of 63 due to a heart attack. .
Mr. Hor Mao's body is being kept for a traditional ceremony in Doeum Chan Village, Sangkat Chbar Ampov II, Khan Chbar Ampov, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Mao was nicknamed the Out-of-Frame Police, where he was active in traffic control at the intersection of Lu Pram Road, Stung Meanchey Sangkat, and later facilitated traffic on National Road 2 in front of Chak Angre Krom Pagoda. Not a few people know Hor Mao through hard work, not afraid of heat, not afraid of rain, facilitate traffic for passengers on the road.
