(Zurich): Austria will release funds to the Palestinian Relief and Employment Agency (UNRWA) after a suspension after its staff were accused of involvement in the October 7 Hassan attack. This is according to the release by Reuters on Saturday, May 18, 2024.
Vienna's decision comes after UNRWA launched an action plan to ensure impartiality, strengthen internal controls and improve the way its staff are monitored. "After a thorough analysis of the plan, we will resubmit funding to UNRWA," the Austrian Foreign Ministry said in a statement. A total of 3.4 million euros ($ 3.70 million) is planned for 2024, with the first payment to be made in the summer.
Austria is one of a number of donors contributing $ 450 million in funding after Israel accused 12 UNRWA staff members of involvement in a war-torn Hamas attack. Gaza Strip. Resolution of the 7th General Assembly of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia.
