Vietnam names Public Security Minister To Lam new President
The Vietnam Central News Agency reports that the party's Central Committee has approved the appointment of To Lam, a member of the Politburo and Minister of Public Security, as the new president. The appointment has been approved by the party's central committee, but will go through a formal election by the National Assembly next week.
Lam, 66, has been the Minister of Public Security since 2016 and is known for his strong stance on the human rights movement in Vietnam.
