(Phnom Penh): Samdech Preah Puth Mony, Dr. Khim Sorn, Representative of the Board of Priests of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Mayor of Phnom Penh, and Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto presided over the closing ceremony of the General Assembly of the Cambodian Buddhist Association. 7 at Chaktomuk Conference Hall on the evening of May 18, 2024.
Please be informed that Mr. Chay Borin, Minister of Cults and Religions and Samdech Preah Mongkul Moni Rainsy Hou Chivneath, Royal Representative of the Board of Priests, presided over the opening ceremony of the 7th General Assembly of the Cambodian Buddhist Association.
In her speech, Ms. Khieu Sina Chea Chanto stated that the Buddhist Association of Cambodia is a very important legacy of Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipadei Choat Nano Chuon Nath, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach 1st Class, Mahanikaya. According to the Ponleu Buddhachak document, Samdech Preah Sangkhareach established the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia in 1952 to serve the interests of monks and Buddhists both inside and outside the country.
In 1965, the Kingdom of Cambodia was honored to host the World Buddhist Leaders' Summit. Also assigned the task of the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia to be directly responsible for organizing the summit at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
The Chaktomuk Conference Hall, which is currently holding the General Assembly of the Buddhist Association of Cambodia, was built on the initiative of Samdech Preah Sangkhareach Chuon Nath Choat Nano and under the patronage of His Majesty King Norodom Sihanouk, Head of State of the Kingdom. Cambodia In order for the work of the Buddhist Association of the State of Cambodia to organize meetings such as subcommittee meetings.
