The election campaign for the fourth mandate council in 2024 will last for eight days from May 17 to 24, 2024. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Attends Lunch with Japanese Ambassador to Cambodia
To begin with, after warmly welcoming Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the leadership of the Senate, the Ambassador of Japan stated that he and his colleagues were very pleased that Samdech Techo had accepted his invitation and attended the dinner. Noon at His Excellency's residence today.
According to his research, Samdech Techo came to the Embassy of Japan in 2004 during the term of Ambassador Fumioki. The Japanese Embassy was built in 2002 when there were not many buildings around. But now there are the buildings of the Cambodian People's Party and the magnificent building of the Ministry of Interior and the buildings around the embassy, which show the great development of Phnom Penh.
Every morning he walks with his wife in the embassy compound and sees photos of the three Samdech (Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet and Samdech Heng Samrin). Yesterday morning, he heard the sound of the election campaign, which made His Excellency aware of the activities of Cambodia's internal politics.
He praised the organization of elections in Cambodia, whether general or non-universal, which is held every five years. Japan has supported Cambodia in holding elections since 1993. These are Japan's contributions to strengthening democracy in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen took over as president of the Cambodian Senate last month. He saw the prince very busy in the field of international relations. Samdech Techo met with Myanmar military chief General Min Oung Liang to receive the King of Brunei Sultan and yesterday to receive a delegation from the French Senate. At the same time, he saw that the Prime Minister was active and busy, as well as the President of the National Assembly.
Peace and stability are very important compared to the current world situation, including the war between Russia and Ukraine, the war in the Middle East, the problems in Myanmar and the problems in Slovakia.
Due to the stability, Japanese companies have invested heavily in Cambodia. He thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for receiving the Toyota representative after the inauguration of the Toyota car assembly plant in Cambodia.
Cambodia is moving faster than Japan in the digital sector. His Excellency was very surprised to see that in Cambodia there is the use of QR codes for payment.
In November 2024, Cambodia will host the Siem Reap-Angkor Summit on "A Mine-Free World". Within this framework, Cambodia and Japan will also cooperate in demining training. In response, Samdech Techo said that he had come to the Japanese Embassy to sign a letter of condolence after the 2011 earthquake in Japan.
Cambodia has been holding regular elections and political parties since 1993. Cambodia has never postponed elections, both nationally and sub-nationally.
The election of senators has been held since the second mandate, as the first mandate is the nomination, followed by the subsequent sub-national elections, the election of commune councils, districts and provinces ....
Samdech Techo It is very good that Japan is helping Cambodia at all stages of the democratic process. He urged the ambassador to see that when the extremist movement is reduced in the region, the democratic situation will improve, including in Cambodia.
According to Samdech's predictions, when the old is over, the young extremists will improve the democratic process. In a democracy there must be no extremist movement, even in France there are concerns about Le Pen's extremist movement. Elections are for the safety of the people, not for war. Extremist movements can lead to war.
Countries are developed, but for Cambodia we have to run while developed countries are moving. In the new government, there are young people who have a high ability to accelerate the digital sector. Crisis has always provided opportunities, Kovid has propelled Cambodia forward five years digitally.
When Kovid School is closed, so we have to use digital to continue teaching activities. In the past, we have used information technology to reform, including governance and taxation.
In that, we paid salaries through the first bank as an acceleration, the second as the fight against corruption, we cut the ghost officials from the list of 20,000 civil servants. In the field of taxation, we have encouraged online and bank tax payments.
Thank you for your assistance and encourage further cooperation in this area. Cambodia can be a place of experience in the digital field.
The Prime Minister and the Japanese Ambassador also exchanged views on regional and international issues, such as the situation in Myanmar, the Middle East war, the Ukraine-Russia war, and the impact on the development of artificial intelligence in the world economy.
Samdech Techo said that war equipment is part of the growth of technology such as bullets, guns, airplanes ... etc. If the world shifts from using technology for war to using it for economic purposes, then the world's growth will be very limited.
At the end, the Ambassador would like to thank Samdech Techo for the honor of coming to His Excellency's residence, including His Excellency the two Vice Presidents, the Secretary General and the Director General of Samdech Techo's Cabinet.
Samdech thanked the Ambassador of Japan for inviting Samdech and his associates of the Senate to this luncheon, which is the first priority for the Ambassador after Samdech took office as President of the Senate.
Finally, I would like to wish Mr. Lim Chea Vutha, Co-Founder and CEO and all the staff of Fresh News Network good health, happiness in the family and success in all tasks and good luck. The five blessings are age, class, happiness, strength, and influence.
Floods kill at least 50 in western Afghanistan
KABUL, May 18 (Xinhua) - Floods triggered by heavy rains killed at least 50 people in the western part of the country just one week after heavy rains, officials in Afghanistan said on Saturday. More than 315 people have died in floods in the north of the country. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency.
Last week, flash floods caused by heavy rains devastated villages in northern Afghanistan, killing 315 people and injuring more than 1,600. Samdech Hun Sen and Lok Chumteav Bandit Conclude Visit to South Korea with Good Results for the Benefit of the Nation and People
(Seoul, South Korea): The Prime Minister of Cambodia, His Excellency Hun Manet, and his wife, Dr. Pech Chanmony Hun Manet, have concluded their official visit to the Republic of Korea, or South Korea, after spending time with the program. Busy for 4 days.
After completing the work program as the agenda of the planned visit of more than 20 programs, Samdech Thipdey and Lok Chumteav Bandith led the delegation to return to Cambodia overnight. His Excellency and Lok Chumteav Bandith led the delegation to leave Seoul at around 4 pm on May 18, 2024.
Please be reminded that at the invitation of South Korean President Yoon Seok-yol, Prime Minister Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Bandit led a delegation to pay their first official visit to South Korea on the morning of the 15th. May 2024.
This confirmation of Samdech Thipadei Hun Manet was made on the occasion that Samdech and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony met with the Cambodian community in the Republic of Korea on the afternoon of May 18, 2024.
Samdech Mani Hun Manet stated that the Cambodian community abroad can provide opportunities for Cambodian children born abroad, and the establishment of many Cambodian communities abroad can make the Khmer language and Khmer culture flourish abroad. Wider and will provide more benefits to the people of Cambodia.
"This is that our policy is not closed, but we have provided additional opportunities, but the sending of workers abroad or our people to study abroad to live abroad, the government does not give up. No, the Cambodian Constitution requires the Royal Government to protect Cambodian citizens everywhere. "So the government's protection policy for the Korean people is that we have done a lot."
Regarding the accusation that the Prime Minister of Cambodia came to brag only about sending Cambodians to work in their homeland, Samdech Hun Manet replied that only countries that block the economy do not allow people to go out. Sending people to work abroad is not uncommon without a mobile population, on the other hand, countries around the world have a mobile labor force.
Hun Manet added that in the phase of globalization, the signing of a free trade agreement aims to facilitate the flow of products, the flow of human capital so that countries that lack labor can recruit labor from other countries. .
At the same time, the Prime Minister mentioned that the benefits that countries send workers receive are to improve the living standards of the people through higher salaries and even skills.
Samdech Hun Sen stressed that opening the door and finding a labor market for people abroad is not about taking workers or taking people as slaves, nor is it forced. Obviously, sending people to work in the country is not to go alone, the Royal Government has a mechanism to support it.
