The announcement of an additional three months for the identification officer was made on the occasion of Samdech Thipdey Hun Manet and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony meeting with the Cambodian community in the Republic of Korea on the afternoon of May 18, 2024.
"I have not yet sent back the identity officer. I have agreed for an additional three months to continue to apply for a passport in Korea. Thank you," said Hun Manet. For the efforts of our identification officers.
"I would like to apologize to all the families of our identification officers who have been waiting for their husbands, fathers and children to return to Cambodia at the end of the month," he said. This is because we have to ask all our officials for another three months to help the people of Korea.
This statement was made on the occasion of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Manet, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Lok Chumteav Dr. Pech Chanmony, meeting with the people of the Khmer community in the Republic of Korea on the afternoon of May 18, 2024.
"The sending of workers to work abroad and students to study abroad is not abandoned by the Royal Government. The Cambodian Constitution requires the protection of Cambodian citizens everywhere, so the protection policy of the Royal Government," he said. "Made for the people of Korea, this is done a lot."
He said that during the 19th Kovid, the Royal Government also worked with the Korean side to support Cambodian workers, while currently the identification officers of the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Labor, and the diplomats of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs were also facilitating the work of the passports. Domain for Cambodian citizens online without any discrimination.
The Prime Minister continued that the work of arranging guest houses for Cambodian workers has also been organized to facilitate workers who need to stay temporarily with the provision of food or rice. In this regard, the Cambodian side has cooperated with the Association in Korea to help provide support to Cambodians in need.
Samdech Hun Manet added that the Cambodian side has cooperated with the Center for Supporting Foreign Workers and the Korean Labor Advisory Center to do some work to help Cambodian workers in Korea. The prince also hopes that this work will continue because there will be more Cambodian workers coming to Korea and there will be people who need help to solve more.
In addition, when Cambodian workers face accidents, the Cambodian Embassy in Korea, Ministry of Labor officials stationed there also cooperated with lawyers and the Korean side to ensure proper procedures for the victims. Compensation for other benefits or handed over to the victim's family (in case of loss of life).
He stressed that the Royal Government will not abandon the Cambodian people no matter where they are, and he advised the Cambodian Embassy in Korea to work hard to help the people.
Minister of Cult and Religion and Samdech Preah Mongkul Moni Rainsy Hou Chhiv Neath open the 7th General Assembly of the Buddhist Association of Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chay Borin, Minister of Cults and Religions, and Samdech Preah Mongkul Moni Rainsy Hou Chivneath, Royal Council of Monks, presided over the opening ceremony of the 7th General Assembly of the Cambodian Buddhist Association on May 18, 2024. At the Chaktomuk Conference Hall.
After that, the Buddhist Association of Cambodia was active in the country and on the international stage, especially training monks to support the social welfare of monks, the people widely spread the teachings of the Buddha. The State Association of Cambodia has played an important role in supporting the field of Buddhism and society.
During 1975, the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia was disbanded, both domestically and internationally, under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. By 1994, the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia was re-established and continued its activities with the support of Buddhist philanthropists.
Currently, the State Buddhist Association of Cambodia has more than 10,000 members, both monks and lay people. Some provinces have already organized their conventions. Some provinces are preparing to hold a general assembly at their provincial level. In order for this association to be sustainable and to continue its relationship with the World Buddhist Association, it is essential that we expand the membership of pagoda branches throughout the country.
Today, the Buddhist Association of the State of Cambodia holds its 7th General Assembly to gather ideas, improve the shortcomings and fill in the gaps and amend some of the provisions of the statute: to respond appropriately to the development of National society and Buddhism.
