During his visit, Samdech Hun Sen met with the Governor of Jeju Province and signed a sisterhood agreement with Siem Reap, especially for direct flights. He added that in the future, he will connect with many other provinces to promote better relations.
According to President Hun Manet, by raising the level of relations between Cambodia and South Korea, it is possible to show that the leaders of Cambodia and Korea share the same vision and give importance to the relationship between the two countries. In this regard, Samdech urged the private sector and the private sector between the two countries to prepare a package of tourist destinations for direct flights.
President Hun Manet expressed the view that the connection of direct flights between the provinces of Korea with Cambodia is to facilitate people and tourists, especially to reduce all travel costs. However, strengthening relations and expanding quotas for people to work in Korea are also equally important.
